INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (22, 10, 'Adam may eat from every tree.', 'Behold, I have given your every herb bearing seed, which is upon the face of all the earth, and every tree ... to you it shall be for meat. Genesis 1:29', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (23, 10, 'There is one tree from which Adam may not eat.', 'But of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it. Genesis 2:17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (24, 11, 'Don''t eat animals. Be a vegan (or at least a vegetarian).', 'And God said, Behold, I have given you every herb bearing seed, which is upon the face of all the earth, and every tree, in the which is the fruit of a tree yielding seed; to you it shall be for meat. Genesis 1:29', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (25, 11, 'Only certain kinds of animals may be eaten.', 'Nevertheless, these shall ye not eat, of them that chew the cud or of them that divide the cloven hoof; as the camel and the hare, and the coney; for they chew the cud, but divide not the hoof; therefore, they are unclean unto you. And the swine, because it divideth the hoof, yet cheweth not the cud, it is unclean unto you; ye shall not eat of their flesh, nor touch their dead carcass. Deuteronomy 14:7-8

These are the beasts which ye shall eat among all the beasts that are on the earth. Whatsoever parteth the hoof, and is clovenfooted, and cheweth the cud, among the beasts, that shall ye eat. Nevertheless these shall ye not eat of them that chew the cud, or of them that divide the hoof: as the camel, because he cheweth the cud, but divideth not the hoof; he is unclean unto you. Leviticus 11:2-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (26, 11, 'Eat anything that moves.', 'Every moving thing that liveth shall be meat for you. Genesis 9:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (27, 11, 'Eat whatever you want. Nothing is unclean, so there''s no need to wash it.', 'And he saith unto them, Are ye so without understanding also? Do ye not perceive, that whatsoever thing from without entereth into the man, it cannot defile him; Because it entereth not into his heart, but into the belly, and goeth out into the draught, purging all meats? And he said, That which cometh out of the man, that defileth the man. Mark 7:18-20, Matthew 15:11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (28, 12, 'Eliphaz''s concubine', 'These are the names of Esau''s sons; Eliphaz, Eliphaz... And Timna was concubine to Eliphaz.... Genesis 36:10-12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (29, 12, 'Eliphaz''s son.', 'The sons of Esau; Eliphaz.....The sons of Eliphaz ... Timnah.... 1 Chronicles 1:35-36', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (30, 12, 'Lotan''s sister', 'These are the sons of Seir the Horite, who inhabited the land; Lotan ... and Lotan''s sister was Timna. Genesis 36:20-22

The sons of Seir; Lotan ... and Timna was Lotan''s sister. 1 Chronicles 1:38-39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (31, 13, 'No, even God has to rest sometimes.', 'And on the seventh day God ended his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had made. 
				        And God blessed the seventh day, and sanctified it: because that in it he had rested from all 
				        his work which God created and made. Genesis 2:2-3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (32, 13, 'Yes. Jesus and his dad always work on the Sabbath.', 'Therefore did the Jews persecute Jesus, and sought to slay him, because he had done these things on the sabbath day. 
				        But Jesus answered them, My Father worketh hitherto, and I work. John 5:16-17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (33, 15, 'One day.', 'These are the  generations of the heavens and of the earth when they were created, in
    			the day that the LORD God made the earth and the heavens. Genesis 2:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (34, 15, 'Six days.', 'And God said, Let there be light: and there was light. ... 
				  And God called the light Day, and the darkness he called Night. And the evening 
				    and the morning were the first day. 
				    ...
				
And God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. And the evening and the
				    morning were the sixth day.
				    
Thus the heavens and the earth were finished, and all the host of them. And on the seventh day God ended his work 
				    which he had made; and he rested
				    on the seventh day from all his work which he had made. Genesis 1:3 - 2:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (35, 16, 'Plants were created before humans.', 'And God said, Let the earth bring forth grass, the herb yielding
			          seed, and the fruit tree yielding fruit after his kind, whose seed is
