			         And out of the ground the LORD God formed every beast of the field, and every fowl of the air; and brought them unto Adam ...
			          but for Adam there was not  found an help meet for him.  Genesis 2:18-20
				  
				  
And the LORD God 
				  caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam, and he slept: and he took one of his ribs, and closed up 
				  the flesh instead thereof; And the rib, which the LORD God had taken from man, made he a woman, 
				  and brought her unto the man. Genesis 2:21-22', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (39, 18, 'Yes, it is good to be married.', 'And the Lord God said, It is not good that the man should be alone; 
