INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (77, 35, 'No, there has never been a just person.', 'For there is not a just man upon earth, that doeth good, and sinneth not. Ecclesiastes 7:20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (78, 35, 'Yes, there have been many.', 'Lot, Noah, Joseph (Mary''s husband), Simeon, John the Baptist, Joseph of Arimathaea, and Cornelius the centurion were all just men.
And delivered just Lot, vexed with the filthy conversation of the wicked. 2 Peter 2:7

She [Wisdom] delivered the just man [Lot]. Wisdom 10:6

Noah was a just man and perfect. Genesis 6:9, Ecclesiasticus 44:17

Then Joseph her husband, being a just man, and not willing to make her a publick example, was minded to put her away privily. Matthew 1:19

Simeon ... was just and devout, waiting for the consolation of Israel. Luke 2:25

For Herod feared John, knowing that he was a just man and an holy. Mark 6:20

And, behold, there was a man named Joseph, a counsellor; and he was a good man, and a just ... he was of Arimathaea. Luke 23:50-51

And they said, Cornelius the centurion, a just man, and one that feareth God. Acts 10:22

Wicked people gnash their teeth, while plotting against just people.

The wicked plotteth against the just, and gnasheth upon him with his teeth. Psalm 37:12
Just people are laughed to scorn.

The just upright man is laughed to scorn. Job 12:4
But their houses are blessed by God.

The curse of the LORD is in the house of the wicked: but he blesseth the habitation of the just. Proverbs 3:33
Just people walk along a shining path towards a perfect day.

But the path of the just is as the shining light, that shineth more and more unto the perfect day. Proverbs 4:18
Just people become more learned with instruction.

Give instruction to a wise man, and he will be yet wiser: teach a just man, and he will increase in learning. Proverbs 9:9
Just people have blessings upon their heads.

Blessings are upon the head of the just: but violence covereth the mouth of the wicked. Proverbs 10:6
The memory of just people is blessed.

The memory of the just is blessed: but the name of the wicked shall rot. Proverbs 10:7
Just people have silver-like tongues.

The tongue of the just is as choice silver. Proverbs 10:20
Just people''s mouths bring forth wisdom.

The mouth of the just bringeth forth wisdom. Proverbs 10:31
Just people are saved by knowledge.

Through knowledge shall the just be delivered. Proverbs 11:9
Just people get out of trouble.

The wicked is snared by the transgression of his lips: but the just shall come out of trouble. Proverbs 12:13
Just people never have anything bad happen to them.

There shall no evil happen to the just. Proverbs 12:21
Just people get sinners stuff when they die.

The wealth of the sinner is laid up for the just. Proverbs 13:22
The condemnation of just people is an abomination to the Lord.

He that justifieth the wicked, and he that condemneth the just, even they both are abomination to the LORD. Proverbs 17:15
Just people should not be punished.

Also to punish the just is not good, nor to strike princes for equity. Proverbs 17:26
Just people walk in integrity and have blessed children.

The just man walketh in his integrity: his children are blessed after him. Proverbs 20:7
Just people love to judge people.

It is joy to the just to do judgment. Proverbs 21:15
Just people fall seven times.

For a just man falleth seven times, and riseth up again: but the wicked shall fall into mischief. Proverbs 24:16
Just people search for the souls of upright people.

The bloodthirsty hate the upright: but the just seek his soul. Proverbs 29:10
Just people think unjust people are abominations.

An unjust man is an abomination to the just: and he that is upright in the way is abomination to the wicked. Proverbs 29:27
Just people perish in their righteousness.

There is a just man that perisheth in his righteousness, and there is a wicked man that prolongeth his life in his wickedness. Ecclesiastes 7:15
Bad things happen to just people.

There is a vanity which is done upon the earth; that there be just men, unto whom it happeneth according to the work of the wicked. Ecclesiastes 8:14
Just people''s paths are upright and are weighed by upright people.

The way of the just is uprightness: thou, most upright, dost weigh the path of the just. Isaiah 26:7
Just people''s blood has been shed by their prophets and priests.

For the sins of her prophets, and the iniquities of her priests, that have shed the blood of the just in the midst of her. Lamentations 4:13
Just people never eat on the mountains.

But if a man be just, and do that which is lawful and right, And hath not eaten upon the mountains. Ezekiel 18:5-6
Just people never defile their neighbor''s wife.

But if a man be just, and do that which is lawful and right, And hath not ... defiled his neighbour''s wife. Ezekiel 18:5-6
Just people never come near a mestruating woman.

But if a man be just, and do that which is lawful and right, and ... neither hath come near to a menstruous woman. Ezekiel 18:5-6
Just people keep all of the commandments.

Hath walked in my statutes, and hath kept my judgments, to deal truly; he is just, he shall surely live, saith the Lord GOD. Ezekiel 18:9
Just people walk in the ways of the Lord.

The ways of the LORD are right, and the just shall walk in them. Hosea 14:9
Just people are afflicted by mighty sins.

For I know your manifold transgressions and your mighty sins: they afflict the just. Amos 5:12
Just people live by faith.

But the just shall live by his faith. Habakkuk 2:4

The just shall live by faith. Romans 1:17, Galatians 3:11, Hebrews 10:38

Just people''s souls are in the hand of God; they shall never be tormented with death.

The souls of the just are in the hand of God, and the torment of death shall not touch them. Wisdom 3:1
Just people condemn the wicked after they die.

The just that is dead, condemneth the wicked that are living. Wisdom 4:16
Just people stand.

Then shall the just stand. Wisdom 5:1
Just people live forever.

The just shall live for evermore. Wisdom 5:16
The course of just people is directed by wisdom.

Wisdom ... directing the course of the just. Wisdom 10:4

She conducted the just. Wisdom 10:10

Just people know Wisdom.

She [Wisdom] knew the just. Wisdom 10:5
Just people are not forsaken by Wisdom.

She [Wisdom] forsook not the just. Wisdom 10:13
Just people are delivered by Wisdom.

She [Wisdom] delivered the just people. Wisdom 10:15
Just people are paid by Wisdom for their labor.

She rendered to the just the wages of their labours. Wisdom 10:17
Just people take the spoils from the wicked.

The just took the spoils of the wicked. Wisdom 10:19
Just people get bread and wine when they are buried.

Lay out thy bread, and thy wine upon the burial of a just man. Tobit 4:18
God sends sunshine and rain on just people.

For he maketh his sun to rise on the evil and on the good, and sendeth rain on the just and on the unjust. Matthew 5:45
Angels will separate the just from the wicked at the end of the world.

So shall it be at the end of the world: the angels shall come forth, and sever the wicked from among the just. Matthew 13:49
Just people will by their wisdom turn fathers'' hearts toward their children.

And he shall go before him in the spirit and power of Elias, to turn the hearts of the fathers to the children, and the disobedient to the wisdom of the just. Luke 1:17
Just people will be resurrected.

But when thou makest a feast, call the poor, the maimed, the lame, the blind: And thou shalt be blessed; for they cannot recompense thee: for thou shalt be recompensed at the resurrection of the just. Luke 14:14

And have hope toward God, which they themselves also allow, that there shall be a resurrection of the dead, both of the just and unjust. Acts 24:15

Just people will be valued 99 times less than repented sinners.

I say unto you, that likewise joy shall be in heaven over one sinner that repenteth, more than over ninety and nine just persons, which need no repentance. Luke 15:7
Only just people can become bishops.

For a bishop must be blameless ... just, holy, temperate. Titus 1:7-8
Just people have perfect spirits.

To the general assembly and church of the firstborn, which are written in heaven, and to God the Judge of all, and to the spirits of just men made perfect. Hebrews 12:23
Just people were killed by rich men.

Go to now, ye rich men, weep and howl for your miseries that shall come upon you. ... Ye have condemned and killed the just; and he doth not resist you. James 5:1-6
Christ suffered for both just and unjust people.

Christ ... suffered for ... the just and the unjust. 1 Peter 3:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (79, 36, 'Yes, God approves of slavery.', 'After the flood, the "just and righteous" Noah (Genesis 6:9, 7:1) got drunk, and lay around naked in his tent. When his son, Ham, saw his father in this condition, Noah cursed not Ham, but Ham''s son, Canaan, and all of Canaan''s descendants, saying, "A servant of servants shall he be unto his brethren." This is one of many Bible passages that have been used to justify slavery.

And he [Noah] said, Cursed be Canaan; a servant of servants shall he be unto his brethren. And he said, Blessed be the LORD God of Shem; and Canaan shall be his servant. God shall enlarge Japheth, and he shall dwell in the tents of Shem; and Canaan shall be his servant. Genesis 9:25-27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (80, 36, 'No, God disapproves of slavery.', 'Love thy neighbor as thyself. Leviticus 19:18, Mark 12:31, Matthew 22:39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (81, 37, 'No, there has never been a righteous person.', 'Since childbirth is a dirty process that involves women, how could any of us be clean or righteous? We can''t and we aren''t. We are all unclean, unrighteous, filthy rags.

What is man, that he should be clean? and he which is born of a woman, that he should be righteous? Job 15:14



We are all as an unclean thing, and all our righteousnesses are as filthy rags. Isaiah 64:6

Who hath declared from the beginning, that we may know? and beforetime, that we may say, He is righteous? yea, there is none that sheweth, yea, there is none that declareth, yea, there is none that heareth your words. Isaiah 41:26

There is none righteous, no, not one. Romans 3:10


Yes, there have been many righteous people.


Abel, Lot, Noah, Daniel, Job, David, Zacharias son of Barachias, Elisabeth, and Zechariah were all righteous people.


Abel offered unto God a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous. Hebrews 11:4

And delivered just Lot, vexed with the filthy conversation of the wicked: (For that righteous man dwelling among them, in seeing and hearing, vexed his righteous soul from day to day with their unlawful deeds;) 2 Peter 2:7-8

Though these three men, Noah, Daniel, and Job, were in it, they should deliver but their own souls by their righteousness, saith the Lord GOD. Ezekiel 14:14, 20

[God] spared not the old world, but saved Noah the eighth person, a preacher of righteousness, bringing in the flood upon the world of the ungodly. 2 Peter 2:5

For thee [Noah] have I seen righteous before me. Genesis 7:1

Therefore the LORD hath recompensed me [David] according to my righteousness; according to my cleanness in his eye sight. 2 Samuel 22:25

They [Elisabeth and Zechariah] were both righteous before God, walking in the commandments and ordinances of the Lord blameless. Luke 1:6

That upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of righteous Abel unto the blood of Zacharias son of Barachias, whom ye slew between the temple and the altar. Matthew 23:35


God knows the way of the righteous.


Therefore the ungodly shall not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous. For the LORD knoweth the way of the righteous: but the way of the ungodly shall perish. Psalm 1:5-6


His eyes are always on them.


The eyes of the LORD are upon the righteous. Psalm 34:15, 1 Peter 3:12


Righteous people rejoice in the Lord.


Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, ye righteous. Psalm 32:11

Rejoice in the LORD, O ye righteous. Psalm 33:1, Psalm 97:12

The voice of rejoicing and salvation is in the tabernacles of the righteous. Psalm 118:15


Their horns will be exalted.


The horns of the righteous shall be exalted. Psalm 75:10


Righteous people are never forsaken and are never hungry.


Yet have I not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed begging bread. Psalm 37:25

The LORD will not suffer the soul of the righteous to famish. Proverbs 10:3

The righteous eateth to the satisfying of his soul. Proverbs 13:25

Among the righteous there is favour. Proverbs 14:9


Whoever hates them will be desolate.


They that hate the righteous shall be desolate. Psalm 34:21


Righteous people will rejoice when they see God''s vengeance; they will wash their feet in wicked people''s blood.


The righteous shall rejoice when he seeth the vengeance: he shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked. Psalm 58:10

The righteous also shall see ... and shall laugh at him. Psalm 52:6


God makes righteous people wise.


He [God] layeth up sound wisdom for the righteous. Proverbs 2:7


He will never allow them to be moved.


He shall never suffer the righteous to be moved. Psalm 55:22


Follow righteous people.


Keep the paths of the righteous. Proverbs 2:20


God loves righteous people.


The LORD loveth the righteous. Psalm 146:9


He tells his secret to them.


His [God''s] secret is with the righteous. Proverbs 3:32


Righteous people''s mouths are wells of life.


The mouth of a righteous man is a well of life. Proverbs 10:11


Righteous people will enter through God''s gate.


This gate of the LORD, into which the righteous shall enter. Psalm 118:20


The rod of the wicked won''t touch righteous people.


The rod of the wicked shall not rest upon the lot of the righteous. Psalm 125:3


Righteous people get paid with life.


The labour of the righteous tendeth to life. Proverbs 10:16


Righteous people''s lips feed people and know what to say.


The lips of the righteous feed many. Proverbs 10:21

The lips of the righteous know what is acceptable. Proverbs 10:32


Righteous people get whatever they want.


The desire of the righteous shall be granted. Proverbs 10:24


Righteous people can smite other people. (It won''t break their heads.)


Let the righteous smite me; it shall be a kindness: and let him reprove me; it shall be an excellent oil, which shall not break my head. Psalm 141:5


When righteous people hope they become glad.


The hope of the righteous shall be gladness. Proverbs 10:28


Righteous people hang around forever.


The righteous shall never be removed. Proverbs 10:30


They are never forgotten.


The righteous shall be in everlasting remembrance. Psalm 112:6


Righteous people get out of trouble.


The righteous is delivered out of trouble. Proverbs 11:8


When things go well with righteous people, the city is happy.


When it goeth well with the righteous, the city rejoiceth. Proverbs 11:10


The children of righteous people will be saved.


The seed of the righteous shall be delivered. Proverbs 11:21


Righteous people want what is good.


The desire of the righteous is only good. Proverbs 11:23


Righteous people grow like a branches.


The righteous shall flourish as a branch. Proverbs 11:28

Righteous people thank God.


The righteous shall give thanks. Psalm 140:13


Righteous people''s fruit is the same as the fruit of the tree of life.


The fruit of the righteous is a tree of life. Proverbs 11:30


Good things happen to righteous people.


The righteous shall be recompensed in the earth. Proverbs 11:31

To the righteous good shall be repayed. Proverbs 13:21


Righteous people''s roots can''t be removed and always yield fruit.


The root of the righteous shall not be moved and always yield fruit. Proverbs 12:3

The root of the righteous yieldeth fruit. Proverbs 12:12


Righteous people are always right.


The thoughts of the righteous are right. Proverbs 12:5

It is not good to ... overthrow the righteous in judgment. Proverbs 18:5


Righteous people''s houses never fall down.


The house of the righteous shall stand. Proverbs 12:7


Righteous people are kind to animals.


A righteous man regardeth the life of his beast. Proverbs 12:10


Righteous people are better than their neighbors.


The righteous is more excellent than his neighbour. Proverbs 12:26


Righteous people hate lying.


A righteous man hateth lying. Proverbs 13:5


Righteous people have happy lights.


The light of the righteous rejoiceth. Proverbs 13:9

Wicked people bow before righteous people.



The evil bow before the good; and the wicked at the gates of the righteous. Proverbs 14:19


Righteous people die hopeful deaths.


The righteous hath hope in his death. Proverbs 14:32


Righteous people have lots of stuff.


In the house of the righteous is much treasure. Proverbs 15:6


Navigation is easy for righteous people.


The way of the righteous is made plain. Proverbs 15:19


Righteous people are safe since they run to the name of the Lord.


The name of the LORD is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe. Proverbs 18:10


Righteous men look at the houses of wicked people.


