Righteous people should not give in to wicked people.


A righteous man falling down before the wicked is as a troubled fountain. Proverbs 25:26


Righteous people are as bold as lions.


The righteous are bold as a lion. Proverbs 28:1


When righteous people rule, everyone is happy.


When the righteous are in authority, the people rejoice. Proverbs 29:2


Righteous people are happy and sing a lot.


The righteous doth sing and rejoice. Proverbs 28:6


Righteous people help the poor.


The righteous considereth the cause of the poor. Proverbs 29:7


When wicked people multiply, bad things happen. But righteous people see the wicked fall.


When the wicked are multiplied, transgression increaseth: but the righteous shall see their fall. Proverbs 29:16


God directs the work of righteous people.


The righteous, and the wise, and their works, are in the hand of God. Ecclesiastes 9:1


The same things happen to righteous and wicked people.


