The sons of Jokshan; Sheba, and Dedan. 1 Chronicles 1:32', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (107, 49, 'Joktan', 'Joktan begat ... Sheba. Genesis 10:26-28, 1 Chronicles 1:20-22', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (108, 50, 'Hebron', 'Then Abraham gave up the ghost ... And his sons Isaac and Ishmael buried him in the cave of Machpelah, in the field of Ephron the son of Zohar the Hittite, which is before Mamre; The field which Abraham purchased of the sons of Heth: there was Abraham buried, and Sarah his wife. Genesis 25:8-10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (109, 50, 'Shechem', 'So Jacob went down into Egypt, and died, he, and our fathers, And were carried over into Shechem, and laid in the sepulchre that Abraham bought for a sum of money of the sons of Emmor the father of Sychem. Acts 7:15-16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (110, 51, 'Raamah', 'The sons of Raamah; Sheba, and Dedan. Genesis 10:7, 1 Chronicles 1:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (111, 51, 'Jokshan', 'Jokshan begat Sheba, and Dedan. Genesis 25:3

The sons of Jokshan; Sheba, and Dedan. 1 Chronicles 1:32', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (112, 52, 'Shem', 'The sons of Shem; Elam, and Asshur, and Arphaxad, and Lud, and Aram, and Uz, and Hul, and Gether, and Meshech. 1 Chronicles 1:17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (113, 52, 'Aram', 'And the children of Aram; Uz, and Hul, and Gether, and Mash. Genesis 10:23', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (114, 53, 'There was only one language.', 'And the whole earth was of one language, and of one speech. Genesis 11:1

And the LORD said, Behold, the people is one, and they have all one language. Go to, let us go down, and there confound their language, that they may not understand one another''s speech. Therefore is the name of it called Babel; because the LORD did there confound the language of all the earth. Genesis 11:6-9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (115, 53, 'There were many languages.', 'By these were the isles of the Gentiles divided in their lands, every one after his tongue. Genesis 10:5

These are the sons of Ham, after their families, after their tongues. Genesis 10:20

These are the sons of Shem, after their families, after their tongues. Genesis 10:31', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (116, 54, 'Salah''s father was Arphaxad', 'And Arphaxad begat Salah. Genesis 10:24
				        
				        And Arphaxad lived five and thirty years, and begat Salah. Genesis 11:12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (117, 54, 'Salah''s father was Cainan.', 'Salah, which was the son of Cainan, which was the son of Arphaxad. Luke 3:35-36', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (118, 55, '145', 'And Terah lived seventy years, and begat Abram. Genesis 11:26
				        
				        Abram was seventy and five years old when he departed out of
				          Haran. Genesis 12:4
				          
				        
The God of glory appeared unto our father Abraham, when he was in Mesopotamia, before he dwelt in Charran. And said unto him, 
				          Get thee out of thy country, and from thy kindred, and come into the land which I shall shew thee. Then came he out of the land of 
				          the Chaldaeans, and dwelt in Charran: and from thence, when his father was dead, 
				          he removed him into this land, wherein ye now dwell.  
				          Acts 7:2-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (119, 55, '205', 'And the days of Terah were two hundred and five years; and
