				        1 Chronicles 23:6
				        
				        
And these are the names of the sons of Levi according to their generations; Gershon, 
				        and Kohath, and Merari. Exodus 6:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (198, 92, '32', 'And these are the names of the children of Israel, which came into Egypt, Jacob and his sons: Reuben [1], Jacob''s firstborn.

And the sons of Reuben; Hanoch [2], and Phallu [3], and Hezron [4], and Carmi [5].

And the sons of Simeon [6]; Jemuel [7], and Jamin [8], and Ohad [9], and Jachin [10], and Zohar [11], and Shaul [12] the son of a Canaanitish woman.

And the sons of Levi [13]; Gershon [14], Kohath [15], and Merari [16].

And the sons of Judah [17]; Er, and Onan, and Shelah [18], and Pharez [19], and Zarah [20]: but Er and Onan died in the land of Canaan. And the sons of Pharez were Hezron [21] and Hamul [22].

And the sons of Issachar [23]; Tola [24], and Phuvah [25], and Job [26], and Shimron [27].

And the sons of Zebulun [28]; Sered [29], and Elon [30], and Jahleel [31].

These be the sons of Leah, which she bare unto Jacob in Padanaram, with his daughter Dinah [32]. Genesis 46:9-15a', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (199, 92, '33', 'These be the sons of Leah, which she bare unto Jacob in Padanaram, with his daughter Dinah: all the souls of his sons and his daughters were thirty and three. Genesis 46:15b', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (200, 93, 'Yes.', 'Neither shalt thou make marriages with them; thy daughter thou shalt not give unto his son, nor his daughter shalt thou take unto thy 
				        son. For they will turn away thy son from following me, that they may serve other gods: so will the anger of the LORD be kindled against you, 
				        and destroy thee suddenly. Deuteronomy 7:3-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (201, 93, 'No, some of God''s favorite people had foreign wives and he didn''t seem to mind.', 'And unto Joseph in the land of Egypt were born Manasseh and Ephraim, which Asenath the daughter of Potipherah priest of On bare unto him. 
				     Genesis 46:20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (202, 94, 'They were the sons of Benjamin', 'And the sons of Benjamin were Belah, and Becher, and Ashbel, Gera, and Naaman, Ehi,
				    and Rosh, Muppim, and Huppim, and Ard. Genesis 46:21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (203, 94, 'They were the grandsons of Benjamin', 'And the sons of Bela were Ard and Naaman. Numbers 26:40', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (204, 95, '70', 'All the souls of the house of Jacob, which came into Egypt,
				          were threescore and ten. Genesis 46:27
				
				        And all the souls that came out of the loins of Jacob were
				          seventy souls. Exodus 1:5
				          
				          
Thy fathers went down into Egypt with threescore and ten persons. Deuteronomy 10:22', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (205, 95, '75', 'Then sent Joseph, and called his father Jacob to him, and all
				          his kindred, threescore and fifteen souls. Acts 7:14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (206, 97, 'Jacob was buried at Machpelah.', 'For his sons carried him into the land of Canaan, and buried him [Jacob] in the cave of the field of Machpelah. Genesis 50:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (207, 97, 'Jacob was buried at Shechem.', 'So Jacob went down into Egypt, and died, he, and our fathers, and were carried over into Shechem, and laid in the sepulchre. Acts 7:15-16

(Shechem is about fifty miles north of Machpelah.)', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (208, 98, 'No.', 'And the king of Egypt called for the midwives, and said unto them, Why have ye done this thing, and have saved the men-children alive? And the midwives said unto Pharaoh, Because the Hebrew women are not as the Egyptian women; for they are lively, and are delivered ere the midwives come in unto them. Therefore God dealt well with the midwives. Exodus 1:18-20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (209, 98, 'Yes.', 'Thou shalt not bear false witness. Exodus 20:16

Thou shalt not raise a false report. Exodus 23:1

Keep thee far from a false matter. Exodus 23:7

Neither lie one to another. Leviticus 19:11

Neither shalt thou bear false witness. Deuteronomy 5:20

Lying lips are an abomination to the Lord. Proverbs 12:22

A righteous man hateth lying. Proverbs 13:5

Deceive not with thy lips. Proverbs 24:28

Wherefore putting away lying, speaking every man truth with his neighbor. Ephesians 4:25

Lie not one to another. Colossians 3:9

Lie not against the truth. James 3:14

All liars shall have their part in the lake which burneth with fire and brimstone. Revelation 21:8

And there shall in no wise enter into it any thing that defileth, neither whatsoever worketh abomination, or maketh a lie: but they which are written in the Lamb''s book of life. Revelation 21:27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (210, 99, 'Moses feared the king.', 'And he said, Who made thee a prince and a judge over us?
				          intendest thou to kill me, as thou killedst the Egyptian? And Moses
				          feared, and said, Surely this thing is known. Now when Pharaoh
				          heard this thing, he sought to slay Moses. But Moses fled from the
				          face of Pharaoh. Exodus 2:14-15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (211, 99, 'Moses did not fear the king.', 'By faith he forsook Egypt, not fearing the wrath of the
				          king: for he endured, as seeing him who is invisible. 
				          Hebrews 11:27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (212, 100, 'God', 'And when the LORD saw that he turned aside to see, God called unto him out of 
				        the midst of the bush, and said, Moses, Moses. Exodus 3:4
				        
				        And as touching the dead, that they rise: have ye not read in the book of Moses, how in the bush God spake unto him, saying, 
				        I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob? Mark 12:26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (213, 100, 'An angel', 'And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, 
				        the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed. Exodus 3:2
				        
				        This Moses whom they refused, saying, Who made thee a ruler and a judge? the same did God send [to be] a ruler and a deliverer 
				        by the hand of the angel which appeared to him in the bush. Acts 7:35', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (214, 101, 'God Almighty', 'I appeared unto Abraham, unto Isaac, and unto Jacob, by the name of God Almighty. Exodus 6:3a', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (215, 101, 'The Lord', 'I am the LORD: that is my name. Isaiah 42:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (216, 101, 'The Lord of hosts', 'I am the LORD thy God, that divided the sea, whose waves roared: The LORD of hosts is his name. Isaiah 51:15

The LORD of hosts is his name. Isaiah 54:5, Jeremiah 31:35, 48:15, 50:34', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (217, 101, 'The Lord God of hosts', 'The LORD, whose name is The God of hosts. Amos 5:27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (218, 101, 'Jehovah', 'My name JEHOVAH - Exodus 6:3b

That men may know that thou, whose name alone is JEHOVAH, art the most high over all the earth. Psalm 83:18

The LORD JEHOVAH is my strength. Isaiah 12:2

in the LORD JEHOVAH is everlasting strength. Isaiah 26:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (219, 101, 'Jealous', 'For thou shalt worship no other god: for the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God. Exodus 34:14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (220, 101, 'JAH', 'Sing unto God, sing praises to his name: extol him that rideth upon the heavens by his name JAH. Psalm 68:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (221, 101, 'I AM THAT I AM', 'And God said unto Moses, I AM THAT I AM: and he said, Thus shalt thou say unto the children of Israel, I AM hath sent me unto you. ... This is my name for ever. Exodus 3:14-15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (222, 102, 'Yes, Moses "was mighty in words."', 'And Moses was learned in all the wisdom of the Egyptians, and was mighty in words and in deeds. 
				        Acts 7:22', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (223, 102, 'No', 'And Moses said unto the LORD, O my LORD, I am not eloquent, neither heretofore, nor 
				      since thou hast spoken unto thy servant: but I am slow of speech, and of a slow tongue. 
				      Exodus 4:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (224, 103, 'God did.', 'And the LORD said unto Moses, When thou goest to return into Egypt,
				          see that thou do all those wonders before Pharaoh, which I have put in
				          thine hand: but I will harden his heart, that he shall not let
				          the people go. Exodus 4:21
				
				        And I will harden Pharaoh''s heart, and multiply my signs and
				          my wonders in the land of Egypt. Exodus 7:3
				
				        
And he hardened Pharaoh''s heart, that he hearkened not unto
				          them; as the LORD had said. Exodus 7:13
				
				        
And the LORD hardened the heart of Pharaoh, and he hearkened
				          not unto them; as the LORD had spoken unto Moses. Exodus 9:12
				 
				        
And the LORD said unto Moses, Go in unto Pharaoh: for I have
				          hardened his heart, and the heart of his servants, that I might
				          shew these my signs before him. Exodus 10:1
				
				        
But the LORD hardened Pharaoh''s heart, so that he would not
				          let the children of Israel go. Exodus 10:20
				
				        
But the LORD hardened Pharaoh''s heart, and he would not let
				          them go. Exodus 10:27
				
				        
And Moses and Aaron did all these wonders before Pharaoh: and the
				          LORD hardened Pharaoh''s heart, so that he would not let the
				          children of Israel go out of his land. Exodus 11:10
				
				        
And I will harden Pharaoh''s heart, that he shall follow after
				          them; and I will be honoured upon Pharaoh, and upon all his host; that
				          the Egyptians may know that I am the LORD. Exodus 14:4
				
				        
And the LORD hardened the heart of Pharaoh king of Egypt, and
				          he pursued after the children of Israel. Exodus 14:8
				
				      
I will harden the hearts of the Egyptians, and they shall follow
				     them: and I will get me honour. Exodus 14:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (225, 103, 'The Pharaoh did.', 'But when Pharaoh saw that there was respite, he hardened his heart. 
				      Exodus 8:15
				      
				      And Pharaoh hardened his heart at this time also, neither would he let the
				    people go. Exodus 8:32
				    
				    
And when Pharaoh saw that the rain and the hail and the thunders were ceased, he sinned 
				    yet more, and hardened his heart, he and his servants. Exodus 9:34
				      
				        
Wherefore then do ye harden your hearts, as the Egyptians and
				          Pharaoh hardened their hearts? 1 Samuel 6:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (226, 104, 'Yes', 'And Abraham called the name of that place Jehovahjireh: as it is said to this day, In the mount of the
				     LORD it shall be seen. Genesis 22:14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (227, 104, 'No', 'And I appeared unto Abraham, unto Isaac, and unto Jacob, by the name of God Almighty, but by my name JEHOVAH was I not known to
				     them. Exodus 6:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (228, 105, 'Gershon', 'The sons of Gershon; Libni, and Shimi, according to their families.Exodus 6:17

And these are the names of the sons of Gershon by their families; Libni, and Shimei. Numbers 3:18

And these be the names of the sons of Gershom; Libni, and Shimei. 1 Chronicles 6:17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (229, 105, 'Mahli', 'The sons of Merari; Mahli, Libni his son, Shimei his son, Uzza his son. 1 Chronicles 6:29', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (230, 106, 'For six days', 'Six days thou shalt eat unleavened bread: and on the seventh day shall be a solemn assembly to the Lord thy God. Deuteronomy 16:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (231, 106, 'For seven days', 'Seven days shall ye eat unleavened bread. Exodus 12:15

Seven days thou shalt eat unleavened bread ... Unleavened bread shall be eaten seven days. Exodus 13:6-7

Thou shalt eat unleavened bread seven days, as I commanded thee. Exodus 23:15

Seven days ye must eat unleavened bread. Leviticus 23:6

Seven days shalt thou eat unleavened bread therewith, even the bread of affliction. Deuteronomy 16:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (232, 107, 'Yes, they were all killed.', 'Behold, the hand of the LORD is upon thy cattle which is in the field, upon the horses, upon 
				       the asses, upon the camels, 
				        upon the oxen, and upon the sheep: there shall be a very grievous murrain. ... And the 
				        LORD did that thing on the morrow, 
				        and all the cattle of Egypt died. Exodus 9:3-6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (233, 107, 'No he saved some to kill later.', 'Send therefore now, and gather thy cattle, and all that thou hast in the field; for upon every man and beast which shall be found in the field, 
				        and shall not be brought home, the hail shall come down upon them, and they shall die. 
				        Exodus 9:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (234, 108, 'God is warlike', 'The Lord is a man of war. Exodus 15:3
				        
				        He teacheth my hands to war. Psalm 18:34
				        
				       
Blessed be the Lord my strength, which teacheth my hands to
				          war, and my fingers to fight.  Psalm 144:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (235, 108, 'God is peaceful', 'The God of Peace Romans 15:33, 16:20; 
				        Hebrews 13:20
				        
				        God is not the author of confusion but of peace. 1 Corinthians 14:33
				        
				        
The God of love and peace. 2 Corinthians 13:11
				        
				       
The Lord of peace himself give you peace always.  2 Thessalonians 3:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (236, 109, 'Yes', 'And it came to pass, as soon as he came nigh unto the camp, that he saw the calf, and 
				        the dancing: and 
				        Moses'' anger waxed hot....  And Moses said unto Aaron, What did this people unto thee, that thou hast 
				        brought so great a sin upon them? ... Thus saith the Lord God of Israel, Put every man his sword by 
				        his side, and go in and out from gate to gate throughout the camp, and slay every man his brother, 
				        and every man his companion, and every man his neighbour. And the children of Levi did according 
				        to the word of Moses: and there fell of the people that day about three thousand men. 
				        Exodus 32:19-28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (237, 109, 'No', 'And Miriam the prophetess, the sister of Aaron, took a timbrel in her hand; and all the women went out after her with
				     timbrels and with dances. And Miriam answered them, Sing ye to the LORD, for he hath triumphed gloriously; the horse and his rider hath he
				     thrown into the sea. Exodus 15:20-21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (238, 110, 'Only the two tables of Moses', 'There was nothing in the ark save the two tables of stone, 
				        which Moses put there at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with 
				        the children of Israel, when they came out of the land of Egypt. 1 Kings 8:9
				
				        There was nothing in the ark save the two tables which Moses put therein 
				        at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when 
				        they came out of Egypt. 2 Chronicles 5:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (239, 110, 'The tables of Moses, a golden pot filled with manna, and Aaron''s budded rod.', 'The ark of the covenant overlaid round about with gold, wherein
				     was the golden pot that had manna, and Aaron''s rod that budded, and the 
				     tables of the covenant. Hebrews 9:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (240, 111, 'The wilderness of Sin in Rephidim', 'And all the congregation of the children of Israel journeyed from the wilderness of Sin, 
				        ... and pitched in Rephidim: and 
				        there was no water for the people to drink. Wherefore the people did chide with Moses, and said, 
				        Give us water that we may drink. ... And the LORD said unto Moses ... I will stand before 
				        thee there upon the rock in Horeb; and thou shalt smite the rock, and there shall come water 
				        out of it, that the people may drink. And Moses did so in the sight of the elders of Israel. ... 
				        And he called the name of the place Massah, and Meribah. Exodus 17:1-7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (241, 111, 'The desert of Zin in Kadesh', 'Then came the children of Israel ... into the desert of Zin in the 
				        first month: and the people abode in Kadesh; and Miriam died there, and was buried there. And there 
				        was no water for the congregation: and they gathered themselves together against Moses and against 
				        Aaron. ... And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying, Take the rod ... and 
						speak ye unto the rock before their eyes; and it shall give forth his 
						water.... Moses lifted up his hand, and with his rod he smote the rock twice: and the water 
				        came out abundantly, and the congregation drank, and their beasts also. Numbers 20:1-8
				        
				        For ye rebelled against my commandment in the desert of Zin, in the strife of the 
				        congregation, to sanctify me at the water before their eyes: that is the water of Meribah
						in Kadesh in the wilderness of Zin.  Numbers 27:14
						
						
Because ye trespassed against me among the children of Israel at the waters of MeribahKadesh, 
						in the wilderness of Zin.... Deuteronomy 32:51', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (242, 112, 'God can''t be tempted.', 'Let no man say when he is tempted, I am tempted of God: for God
					          cannot be tempted with evil, neither tempteth he any man. James 1:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (243, 112, 'God can be tempted.', 'Ye shall not tempt the Lord your God. Deuteronomy 6:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (244, 113, 'By smiting it.', 'And the LORD said unto Moses, Go on before the people, and take with thee of the elders of Israel; and thy rod, 
				        wherewith thou smotest the river, take in thine hand, and go. Behold, I will stand before thee there upon the rock in Horeb; 
				        and thou shalt smite the rock, and there shall come water out of it, that the people may drink. ... 
				        And he called the name of the place Massah, and Meribah. Exodus 17:5-7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (245, 113, 'By talking to it.', 'And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying, Take the rod, and gather thou the assembly together, thou, and Aaron thy brother, 
				        and speak ye unto the rock before their eyes; and it shall give forth his water. Numbers 20:7-8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (246, 113, 'By using the Umim and Thumim.', 'Thy Thummim and thy Urim ... thou didst prove at Massah, and ... at the waters of Meribah. Deuteronomy 33:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (247, 114, 'Jethro', 'Now Moses kept the flock of Jethro his father in law. Exodus 3:1
				    
				    And Moses went and returned to Jethro his father in law. Exodus 4:18
				    
				    
When Jethro, the priest of Midian, Moses'' father in law.... Exodus 18:1
				    
				    
And Jethro Moses'' father in law, came with his sons and  his wife unto Moses. Exodus 18:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (248, 114, 'Hobab', 'Now Heber the Kenite, which as of the children of Hobab
				          the father in law of Moses. Judges 4:11
				          
				    And Moses said unto Hobab, the son of Raguel the Midianite, Moses'' father in law.... Numbers 10:29', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (249, 114, 'Reuel', 'Reuel ... gave Moses Zipporah his daughter. Exodus 2:18-21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (250, 115, 'Yes, at least when they are designed and commissioned by God.', 'And the Lord spake unto Moses, saying, ... Thou shalt make two cherubims of gold ... And the cherubims
				          shall stretch forth their wings on high, covering the mercy seat with
				          their wings, and their faces shall look to one another. Exodus 25:1, 
				          18-20
				          
				          Thou shalt make ... with cherubims of cunning work. Exodus 26:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (251, 115, 'No, graven images are abominations to God.', 'Thou shalt not make unto thee any graven image, or any
				          likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth
				          beneath. Exodus 20:4, Deuteronomy 5:8
				          
				        Lest ye corrupt yourselves, and make you a graven image, the
				          simultude of any figure, the likeness of male or female, The likeness
				          of any beast that is on the earth, the likeness of any winged fowl
				          that flieth in the air, The likeness of any thing that creepeth on the
				          ground, the likeness of any fish that is in the waters beneath the
				          earth. Deuteronomy 4:16-18
				          
				        
Take heed unto yourselves, lest ye forget ... and make you a
				          graven image, or the likeness of any thing, which the Lord thy God
				          hath forbidden thee. Deuteronomy 4:23
				          
				        
Cursed be the man that maketh any graven or molten image, an abomination unto the LORD, 
				        the work of the hands of the craftsman. Deuteronomy 27:15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (252, 116, 'Honor, respect, and obey your parents.', 'Exodus 20:12 — "Honour thy father and thy mother: that thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee." Deuteronomy 5:16 — "Honour thy father and thy mother, as the LORD thy God hath commanded thee; that thy days may be prolonged, and that it may go well with thee, in the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee." Proverbs 1:8 — "My son, hear the instruction of thy father, and forsake not the law of thy mother." Proverbs 23:22 — "Hearken unto thy father that begat thee, and despise not thy mother when she is old." Ephesians 6:2 — "Honour thy father and mother; which is the first commandment with promise."', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (253, 116, 'Disrespect and hate your parents.', 'Matthew 23:9 — "And call no man your father upon the earth: for one is your Father, which is in heaven." Luke 9:59-60 — "And he said unto another, Follow me. But he said, Lord, suffer me first to go and bury my father. Jesus said unto him, Let the dead bury their dead: but go thou and preach the kingdom of God." Luke 14:26 — "If any man come to me, and hate not his father, and mother, and wife, and children, and brethren, and sisters, yea, and his own life also, he cannot be my disciple." John 2:3-4 — "And when they wanted wine, the mother of Jesus saith unto him, They have no wine. Jesus saith unto her, Woman, what have I to do with thee? mine hour is not yet come."', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (254, 117, 'Yes.', 'Thou shalt not commit adultery.   Exodus 20:14, 
				  Deuteronomy 5:18
				  
				  Abstain from ... fornication. Acts 15:20
				  
				  
It is reported commonly that there is fornication among you. 1 Corinthians 5:1
				
				  
The body is not for fornication. 1 Corinthians 6:13
				
				  
Flee fornication. 1 Corinthians 6:18
				  
				    
Neither let us commit fornication. 1 Corinthians 10:8
				
				  
And lest, when I come again, my God will humble me among you, and that I shall bewail many which have
				   sinned already, and have not repented of the uncleanness and fornication and lasciviousness which they 
				   have committed. 2 Corinthians 12:21
				
				  
Now the works of the flesh are manifest, which are these; Adultery, fornication, ... they which do 
				  such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God. Galatians 5:19-21
				  
				    
But fornication, ... let it not be once named among you. 
				    Ephesians 5:3
				
				  
Mortify therefore your members which are upon the earth; fornication, ..., For which things'' 
				  sake the wrath of God cometh on the children of disobedience. Colossians 3:5-6
				
				  
Ye should abstain from fornication. 1Thessalonians 4:3
				  
				      
Whoremongers and adulterers God will judge. Hebrews 13:4
				  
				    
Even as Sodom and Gomorrha, and the cities about them in like manner, giving themselves 
				    over to fornication, and going after strange flesh, are set forth for an example, suffering 
				    the vengeance of eternal fire. Jude 7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (255, 117, 'No, fornication and adultery are OK when God commands it.', 'And the Lord said to Hosea, Go, take unto thee a wife of
				          whoredoms.... Hosea 1:2
				
				        Then said the Lord unto me, God yet, love a woman beloved of
				          her friend, yet an adulteress. Hosea 3:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (256, 118, 'Yes, some things you should covet.', 'Wherefore, brethren, covet to prophesy. 1 Corinthians 14:39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (257, 118, 'Don''t covet.', 'Thou shalt not covet. Romans 7:7, 13:9
					        
					        But ... covetousness, let it not be once named among you. Ephesians 5:3
					        
					        
Mortify therefore your members which are upon the earth; fornication, uncleanness, 
					        inordinate affection, evil concupiscence, and covetousness, which is idolatry. Colossians 3:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (258, 119, 'Moses received the law directly from God.', 'And the LORD came down upon mount Sinai, on the top of the mount: and the LORD called Moses up to the top of the mount; and Moses went up. . . . And the LORD said unto Moses, Thus thou shalt say unto the children of Israel, 
				        Ye have seen that I have talked with you from heaven. Exodus 19:20, 20:22', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (259, 119, 'Angels gave the law to Moses through the hand of a mediator.', 'Wherefore then serveth the law? It was added because of transgressions, till the seed should come to whom the promise was made; 
				        and it was ordained by angels in the hand of a mediator. Galatians 3:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (260, 120, 'Love and be kind to them.', 'The stranger that dwelleth with you shall be unto you as one born among you, and thou shalt love him as thyself. Leviticus 19:34

Love ye therefore the stranger. Deuteronomy 10:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (261, 120, 'Kill them.', 'And when the LORD thy God shall deliver them before thee; thou shalt smite them, and utterly destroy them; thou shalt make no covenant with them, nor shew mercy unto them. Deuteronomy 7:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (262, 121, 'Yes, only God is holy.', 'For thou alone are holy. Revelation 15:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (263, 121, 'No, others are holy too.', 'Ye shall be holy men unto me. Exodus 22:31  
				      
				     Ye shall be holy; for I am holy. Leviticus 11:44-45
				      
				      
Ye shall be holy: for I the LORD your God am holy. Leviticus 19:2
				      
				      
Be ye holy; for I am holy. 1 Peter 1:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (264, 122, 'Love them, be kind to them, and treat them well.', 'If thou meet thine enemy''s ox or 
				  his ass going astray, thou shalt surely bring it back to him again. Exodus 23:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (265, 122, 'Hate them and wish them evil.', 'Let their way be dark and slippery: and let the angel of the LORD
				     persecute them. ... Let destruction come upon him at unawares. 
				     Psalm 35:6-8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (266, 123, 'Don''t worry about it. God will kill or drive them out for you.', 'And I will send hornets before thee, which shall drive out the Hivite, the Canaanite, and the Hittite, from before thee.
				
				I will not drive them out from before thee in one year; lest the land become desolate, and the beast of the field multiply against thee.
				
				By little and little I will drive them out from before thee, until thou be increased, and inherit the land.
				
				... They shall not dwell in thy land. Exodus 23:28-32
				        
				     
				And I will send an angel before thee; and I will drive out the Canaanite, the Amorite, and the Hittite, 
				and the Perizzite, 
				the Hivite, and the Jebusite. Exodus 33:2
				
				
 I drive out before thee the Amorite, and the Canaanite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, and 
				the Hivite, and the Jebusite. Exodus 34:11
				
				
 Then will the LORD drive out all these nations from before you, and ye shall possess greater nations 
				and mightier than 
				yourselves. Deuteronly 11:23
				
				
And Joshua said, Hereby ye shall know that the living God is among you, and that he will without fail
				 drive out from before you the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Hivites, and the Perizzites, and 
				 the Girgashites, and the Amorites, and the Jebusites. Joshua 3:10
				 
				 
All the inhabitants of the hill country from Lebanon unto Misrephothmaim, and all the Sidonians, 
				 them will I drive out from before the children of Israel: only divide thou it by lot unto the Israelites 
				 for an inheritance, as I have commanded thee. Joshua 13:6
				 
				 
And the LORD your God, he shall expel them from before you, and drive them from out of your sight; 
				 and ye shall possess their land, as the LORD your God hath promised unto you. 
				 Joshua 23:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (267, 123, 'Kill them all without mercy.', 'When the LORD thy God shall bring thee into the land whither thou goest to possess it, 
				  and hath cast out many nations before thee, the Hittites, and the Girgashites, and the Amorites, 
				  and the Canaanites, and the Perizzites, and the Hivites, and the Jebusites, 
				  seven nations greater and mightier than thou; And when the LORD thy God shall deliver them before thee; 
				  thou shalt smite them, and utterly destroy them; thou shalt make no covenant with them, nor shew mercy 
				  unto them.  Deuteronomy 7:1-2 
				  
				 But of the cities of these people, which the LORD thy God doth give thee for an inheritance, thou shalt 
				save alive nothing that breatheth: But thou shalt utterly destroy them; namely, the Hittites, and the 
				Amorites, the Canaanites, and the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites; as the LORD thy God hath 
				commanded thee. Deuteronomy 20:16-17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (268, 123, 'Drive them out of Canaan.', 'When ye are passed over Jordan into the land of Canaan; Then ye shall drive out all the 
				    inhabitants of the land from before you, and destroy all their pictures, and destroy all their molten 
				    images, and quite pluck down all their high places: And ye shall dispossess the inhabitants of the land, 
				    and dwell therein: for I have given you the land to possess it.
				    Numbers 33:51-53', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (269, 123, 'Welcome them as fellow citizens with the same rights as Israelites.', 'And it shall come to pass, that ye shall divide it by lot for an inheritance unto you,
				 and to the strangers that sojourn among you, which shall beget children among you: 
				 and they shall be unto you as born in the country among the children of Israel; they 
				 shall have inheritance with you among the tribes of Israel. Ezekiel 47:22', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (270, 124, 'God commanded the Israelites to make him burnt offerings.', 'We will go three days'' journey into the wilderness, and sacrifice to the LORD our God, 
				        as he shall command us. Exodus 8:27
				        
				        And Moses said, Thou must give us also sacrifices and burnt offerings,
				    that we may sacrifice unto the LORD our God. Exodus 10:25
				    
				        
An altar of earth thou
				    shalt make unto me, and shalt sacrifice thereon thy burnt offerings, and thy
				    peace offerings, thy sheep, and thine oxen: in all places where I record my
				    name I will come unto thee, and I will bless thee. Exodus 20:24
				    
				        
And you shall kill the ram, and you shall take its blood and
				          sprinkle it all around the altar. Then you shall cut the ram in
				          pieces, wash its entrails and its legs, and put them with its pieces
				          and with its head. And you shall burn the whole ram on the altar It
				          is a burnt offering to the Lord; it is a sweet aroma, an offering made
				          by fire to the Lord. Exodus 29:16-18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (271, 124, 'God did not ask for any burnt offerings.', 'Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Put your burnt offerings unto your sacrifices, and eat flesh. 
				        For I spake not unto your fathers, nor commanded them in the
				          day that I brought them out of the land of Egypt, concerning burnt
				          offerings or sacrifices. Jeremiah 7:21-22', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (272, 125, 'A bullock and two lambs', 'Thou shalt offer every day a bullock for a sin offering for atonement ... 
				Now this is that which thou shalt offer upon the altar; two lambs of the first year day by day continually. 
				The one lamb thou shalt offer in the morning; and the other lamb thou shalt offer at even. Exodus 29:36-39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (273, 125, 'Two lambs (without a bullock)', 'The LORD spake unto Moses, saying ... This is the offering made by fire which ye shall offer unto the LORD; 
				two lambs of the first year without spot day by day, for a continual burnt offering. 
				The one lamb shalt thou offer in the morning, and the other lamb shalt thou offer at even. Numbers 28:1-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (274, 127, 'Yes, God likes censuses.', 'And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying, When thou takest the sum of the children of Israel after their number,
			  then shall they give every man a ransom for his soul unto the LORD, when thou numberest them; that there be no plague 
			  among them, when thou numberest them. 
			  Exodus 30:11-12
			 
			 
And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the tabernacle of the congregation, on the 
			 first day of the second month, in the second year after they were come out of the land of Egypt,
			  saying, Take ye the sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel. 
			  Numbers 1:1-2
			  
			  
And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, saying, 
			  Number the children of Levi after the house of their fathers, by their families: 
			  every male from a month old and upward shalt thou number them. And Moses numbered 
			  them according to the word of the LORD, as he was commanded. Numbers 3:14-16
			  
			  
And the LORD said unto Moses, Number all the firstborn of the males of the
				    children of Israel from a month old and upward, and take the number of their
				    names. Numbers 3:40
			  
			  
And it came to pass after the plague, that the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest, saying,
			  Take the sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel, from twenty years old and upward. 
			  Numbers 26:1-2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (275, 127, 'No. God killed 70,000 men because of David''s census.', 'And again the anger of the LORD was kindled against Israel, and he moved David against them to say, Go, number Israel and Judah. ... 
			        And David''s heart smote him after that he had numbered the people. And David said unto the LORD, I have sinned greatly in that I have done. ...
			        So the LORD sent a pestilence upon Israel ... and there died of the people ... seventy thousand men. 2 Samuel 24:1-17
			        
			        And David said to Joab and to the rulers of the people, Go, number Israel from Beersheba even to Dan; and bring the number of them to
			         me, that I may know it. ... And God was displeased with this thing; therefore he smote Israel. ... So the LORD sent pestilence upon Israel: 
			         and there fell of Israel seventy thousand men. 1 Chronicles 21:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (276, 128, 'Yes', 'Ointment and perfume rejoice the heart. Proverbs 27:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (277, 128, 'No', 'As for the perfume which thou shalt make, ye shall not make to yourselves ... it shall be unto thee holy for the LORD. Exodus 30:37', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (278, 129, 'God never gets tired.', 'Hast thou not known? hast thou not heard, that the everlasting
 			         God, the Lord, the Creator of the ends of the earth, fainteth not,
         				 neither is he weary? Isaiah 40:28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (279, 129, 'Sometimes God gets tired.', 'He was tired after the creation.
					 
					  
					        For in six days the Lord made heaven and earth, and on the
					          seventh day he rested, and was refreshed. Exodus 31:17

					          
					   He is weary of people and their iniquities.					       
					  
					        
					I am weary to bear them. Isaiah 1:14
					
					        Thou has wearied me with thine iniquities. Isaiah 43:24
					        
					        
Ye have wearied the LORD with  your words. Malachi 2:17

					        

					        
					        
					    And he is weary with repenting.				    
					
					        I am weary with repenting. Jeremiah 15:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (280, 130, 'On Mount Sinai.', 'And he gave unto Moses, when he had made an end of communing with him upon mount Sinai, 
				        two tables of testimony, tables of stone, written with the finger of God. Exodus 31:18
				        
				        And he hewed two tables of stone like unto the first; and Moses rose up early in the 
				        morning, and went up unto mount Sinai, as the LORD had commanded him, and took in his hand 
				        the two tables of stone. Exodus 34:4
				        
				        
And afterward all the children of Israel came nigh: and he gave them in
				        commandment all that the LORD had spoken with him in mount Sinai. Exodus 34:32
				        
				        
These are the statutes and judgments and laws, which the LORD made between him and the 
				        children of Israel in mount Sinai by the hand of Moses. Leviticus 26:46
				        
				        
These are the commandments, which the LORD commanded Moses for the children of Israel 
				        in mount Sinai. Leviticus 27:34
				        
				        
Thou camest down also upon mount Sinai, and spakest with them from heaven, and gavest 
				        them right judgments, and true laws, good statutes and commandments. Nehemiah 9:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (281, 130, 'On Mount Horeb.', 'These are the words of the covenant, which the LORD commanded Moses to make with the children 
				        of Israel in the land of Moab, beside the covenant which he made with them in Horeb. 
				        Deuteronomy 29:1
				        
				        There was nothing in the ark save the two tables of stone, which Moses put there at Horeb, 
				        when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of the land 
				        of Egypt. 1 Kings 8:9
				        
				        
There was nothing in the ark save the two tables which Moses put therein at Horeb. 2 Chronicles 5:10
				        
				        
Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb. Malachi 4:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (282, 131, 'Yes (at least he promised to destroy them all)', 'And I will send an angel before thee; and I will drive out the
          Canaanite, the Amorite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite,
          the Hivite, and the Jebusite. Exodus 33:2
          
          When the Lord thy God shall bring thee into the land whither
          thou goest to possess it, and hath cast out many nations before thee,
          the Hittites, ... and the Amorites, and the Canaanites,
          and the Perizzites, and the Jebusites. Deuteronomy 7:1
          
          And he shall deliver their kings into thine hand, and thou
          shalt destroy their name from under heaven: there shall no man be
          able to stand before thee, unto thou have destroyed them. Deuteronomy 7:24
          
          The Lord thy God, he will go over before thee, and he will
          destroy these nations from before thee, and thou shalt possess
          them. Deuteronomy 31:3

          Every place that the sole of your foot shall tread upon, that
          have I given unto you, as I said unto Moses. All the land of the Hivites.
          There shall not any man be able to stand before thee. Joshua 1:3-5
          
          Hereby ye shall know that the living God is among you, and
          that he will without fail drive out from before you the Canaanites,
          and the Hittites, and the Hivites, and the Perizzites,
          ... and the Amorites, and the Jebusites. Joshua 3:10

          For thou shalt drive out the Canaanites, though they
          have iron chariots, and though they be strong. Joshua 17:17-18
          
          And the Lord gave unto Israel all the land which he sware to
          give unto their fathers; and they possessed it, and dwelt therein. And
          there stood not a man of all their enemies before them; the Lord
          delivered all their enemies into their hand. Joshua 21:43-44', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (283, 131, 'No, there were some nations he couldn''t destroy.', 'As for the Jebusites the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the
          children of Judah could not drive them out: but the Jebusites dwell
          with the children of Judah at Jerusalem unto this day. Joshua 15:63
          
          And they drave not out the Cananites that dwell in
          Gezer: but the Canaanites dwell among the Ephraimites unto this
          day. Joshua 16:10
          
          Yet the children of Manasseh could not drive out the
          inhabitants of those cities; but the Canaanites would dwell in
          that land ... The children of Israel ... did not utterly drive them
          out. Joshua 17:12-13
          
          An the children of Benjamin did not drive out the Jebusites
          that inhabited Jerusalem; but the Jebusites dwell with the children of
          Benjamin in Jerusalem unto this day. Judges 1:21

          Neither did Manasseh drive out the inhabitants of Bethshean
          and her towns, ... But the Canaanites would dwell in that land.
          And it cam to pass ... that they ... did not utterly drive them
          out. Judges 1:27-36

          Now these are the nations which the Lord left ... the Canaanites,
          Hittites, and Amorites, and Perizzites, and Hivites,
          and Jebusites. Judges 3:1-5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (284, 132, 'Yes.', 'And the LORD spake unto Moses face to face, as a man speaketh unto his friend. Exodus 33:11
				        
				        And there arose not a prophet since in Israel like unto Moses,
				          whom the Lord knew face to face. Deuteronomy 34:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (285, 132, 'No, he only saw his back parts.', 'Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live. And the LORD said, 
				        Behold, there is a place by me, and thou shalt stand upon a rock: And it shall come to pass, 
				        while my glory passeth by, that I will put theein a clift of the rock, and will cover thee 
				        with my hand while I pass by: And I will take away mine hand, and thou shalt see my back 
				        parts: but my face shall not be seen. Exodus 33:20-23', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (286, 133, 'God', 'And the LORD said unto Moses, Hew thee two tables of stone like unto the first: and 
					        I will write upon
					    these tables the words that were in the first tables, which thou brakest. Exodus 34:1
					    
					    And he wrote on the tables, according to the first writing, the ten
				    commandments, which the LORD spake unto you in the mount out of the midst of
				    the fire in the day of the assembly: and the LORD gave them unto me. Deuteronomy 10:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (287, 133, 'Moses', 'And the LORD said unto Moses, Write thou these words ... And he wrote upon the tables the words of the covenant, the ten
					    commandments. Exodus 34:27-28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (288, 134, 'God is kind, merciful, and good.', 'The LORD God, merciful and gracious, longsuffering, and abundant in goodness and truth. Exodus 34:6

For the Lord thy God is a merciful God. Deuteronomy 4:31

Let us fall now into the hand of the LORD; for his mercies are great. 2 Samuel 24:14

O give thanks unto the Lord; for he is good; for his mercy endureth forever. 1 Chronicles 16:34; Psalm 106:1, 107:1, 118:1, 136:1

Good and upright is the Lord. Psalm 25:8

For thou, Lord, art good, and ready to forgive; and plenteous in mercy unto all them that call upon thee. Psalm 86:5

For the Lord is good, his mercy is everlasting. Psalm 100:5

The Lord is merciful and gracious, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy. Psalm 103:8

The Lord is good to all, and his tender mercies are over all his works. Psalm 145:9

I will not cause mine anger to fall upon you: for I am merciful, saith the LORD, and I will not keep anger for ever. Jeremiah 3:12

The LORD is good; for his mercy endureth for ever. Jeremiah 33:11

For he doth not afflict willingly nor grieve the children of men. Lamentations 3:33

For he is gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness. Joel 2:13

Who is a God like unto thee, that pardoneth iniquity, and passeth by the transgression of the remnant of his heritage? he retaineth not his anger for ever, because he delighteth in mercy. Micah 7:18

Give all of you glory to him, because he is good, because his mercy endureth for ever. Judith 13:21

Blessed be God ... the Father of mercies. 2 Corinthians 1:3

For the Lord is very pitiful and of tender mercy. James 5:11

God is love. 1 John 4:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (289, 134, 'God is cruel, unmerciful, and evil.', 'The Lord God ... visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children, and upon the children''s children, unto the third and to the fourth generation. Exodus 34:6-7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (290, 135, 'They should be exiled.', 'Ye shall keep the sabbath therefore; for it is holy unto you ... for whosoever doeth any work therein, that soul 
       					 shall be cut off from among his people. Exodus 31:14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (291, 135, 'They should be killed.', 'Ye shall keep the sabbath therefore; for it is holy unto you: every one that defileth it 
				    shall surely be put to death. Exodus 31:14
				 
				       Whosoever doeth any work in the sabbath day, he shall surely be put to death. Exodus 31:15
				
				       
Six days shall work be
				    done, but on the seventh day there shall be to you an holy day, a sabbath of
				    rest to the LORD: whosoever doeth work therein shall be put to death. Exodus 35:2
				    
				       
And while the children of Israel were in the wilderness, they found a man that
				    gathered sticks upon the sabbath day. ... And the LORD said unto
				    Moses, The man shall be surely put to death: all the congregation
				    shall stone him with stones without the camp. And all the
				    congregation brought him without the camp, and stoned him with stones, and
				    he died; as the LORD commanded Moses. Numbers 15:32-36', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (292, 136, 'Moses.', 'At that time the LORD said unto me [Moses], Hew thee two tables of stone like unto
				    the first, and come up unto me into the mount, and make thee an ark of wood. ... And I made an ark of 
				    shittim wood.... Deuteronomy 10:1-3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (293, 136, 'Bezaleel.', 'And Bezaleel made the ark of shittim wood. Exodus 37:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (294, 137, 'Kill a young bull.', 'And if the whole congregation of Israel sin through ignorance, and the thing be hid from the eyes of the assembly, 
					    and they have done somewhat against any of the commandments of the Lord concerning things which should not be done, and are guilty;
					
					When the sin, which they have sinned against it, is known, then the congregation shall offer 
							a young bullock for the sin, and bring him before the tabernacle of the congregation.
					
					And the elders of the congregation shall lay their hands upon the head of the bullock before the Lord: and the bullock 
					shall be killed before the Lord.
					
					And the priest that is anointed shall bring of the bullock''s blood to the tabernacle of the congregation:
					
					And the priest shall dip his finger in some of the blood, and sprinkle it seven times before the Lord, even before the vail.
					
					And he shall put some of the blood upon the horns of the altar which is before the Lord, that is in the tabernacle of the congregation, 
					and shall pour out all the blood at the bottom of the altar of the burnt offering, which is at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
					
					And he shall take all his fat from him, and burn it upon the altar.
					
					And he shall do with the bullock as he did with the bullock for a sin offering, so shall he do with this: and the priest shall make an 
					atonement for them, and it shall be forgiven them.
					
					And he shall carry forth the bullock without the camp, and burn him as he burned the first bullock: it is a sin offering for the congregation. 
					Leviticus 4:13-21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (295, 137, 'Kill a young bull and a young goat.', 'Then it shall be, if ought be committed by ignorance without the knowledge of the congregation, that all the congregation shall offer 
						one young bullock for a burnt offering, for a sweet savour unto the Lord, with his meat offering, and his drink offering, 
						according to the manner, and one kid of the goats for a sin offering.
				
					And the priest shall make an atonement for all the congregation of the children of Israel, and it shall be forgiven them; 
					for it is ignorance: and they shall bring their offering, a sacrifice made by fire unto the Lord, and their sin offering before the 
					Lord, for their ignorance:
					
					And it shall be forgiven all the congregation of the children of Israel, and the stranger that sojourneth among them; 
					seeing all the people were in ignorance. Numbers 15:24-26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (296, 138, 'Yes', 'I have given it to you upon the altar to make an atonement for
				          your souls: for it is the blood that maketh an atonement for the
				          soul. Leviticus 17:11
				
				      And if any soul sin through ignorance, then he shall bring a she goat of the first year for a sin
				    offering. And the priest shall make an atonement for the soul that sinneth ignorantly, when he sinneth by ignorance
				    before the LORD, to make an atonement for him; and it shall be forgiven him. Numbers 15:27-28
				
				        
And one kid of the goats for a sin offering: to make an
				          atonement for you. Numbers 29:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (297, 138, 'No', 'For it is not possible that the blood of bulls and of goats
				          should take away sins. Hebrews 10:4
				
				        And every priest standeth daily ministering and offering
				          oftentimes the same sacrifices, which can never take away sins. Hebrews 10:11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (298, 139, 'Kill an unblemished bullock.', 'If a soul shall sin through ignorance ...  let him bring for his sin, which he hath sinned, a young bullock without blemish unto the LORD for a sin offering.
				    Leviticus 4:3-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (299, 139, 'Kill an unblemished ram.', 'If a soul commit a trespass, and sin through ignorance, in the holy things of the LORD; then he shall bring for his trespass unto the LORD a ram without blemish 
				   		out of the flocks ... and the priest shall make an atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering, and it shall be forgiven him.
				      Leviticus 5:15-16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (300, 139, 'Kill a young female goat.', 'And if any soul sin through ignorance, then he shall bring a she goat of the first year for 
				      a sin offering. And the priest shall make an atonement for the soul that sinneth ignorantly, 
				      when he sinneth by ignorance before the Lord, to make an atonement for him; and it shall be 
				      forgiven him. Numbers 15:27-28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (301, 140, 'All are unclean and may not be eaten.', 'And every creeping thing that flieth is unclean unto you: 
				     they shall not be eaten. Deuteronomy 14:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (302, 140, 'Some may be eaten.', 'Yet these may ye eat of every flying creeping thing that goeth upon all
					four, which have legs above their feet, to leap withal upon the earth;
					Even these of them ye may eat; the locust after his kind, and the bald
					locust after his kind, and the beetle after his kind, and the grasshopper
					after his kind. But all other flying creeping things, which have four feet, shall be an abomination unto you.
					Leviticus 11:21-23', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (303, 141, 'Only Levites in the tablenacle', 'Sacrifices are to be done only by Levites.
					     
			And I, behold, I have taken your brethren the Levites from among the children of Israel:
				to you they are given as a gift for the LORD, to do the service of the tabernacle of the
				congregation. Therefore thou and thy sons with thee shall keep your priest''s office for
				everything of the altar, and within the vail; and ye shall serve: I have
				given your priest''s office unto you as a service of gift: and the stranger
			    that cometh nigh shall be put to death. And the LORD spake unto Aaron, Behold, 
				I also have given thee the charge of mine
				heave offerings of all the hallowed things of the children of Israel; unto thee have I given
				them by reason of the anointing, and to thy sons, by an ordinance for ever. 
				Numbers 18:6-8
			
					    
			In the tabernacle
					    
			And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying, Speak unto Aaron, and unto his 
	        	sons, and unto all the children of Israel, and say unto them ... What man ... that 
	     		killeth an ox, or lamb, or goat, in the camp, or that killeth it out of the camp,
				And bringeth it not unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, to offer an offering unto the LORD before the
	     		tabernacle of the LORD; blood shall be imputed unto that man; he hath shed blood; and that man shall be cut off from
	     		among his people: To the end that the children of Israel may bring their sacrifices, which they offer in the open field, 
	     		even that they may bring
	     		them unto the LORD, unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, unto the priest, and offer them for peace
	     		offerings unto the LORD. Leviticus 17:1-5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (304, 141, 'Non-Levites may offer sacrifices away from the tabernacle.', 'Elkanah, Samuel''s father, was an Ephrathite 
	   		 (a member of the tribe of Judah), not a Levite.
	    
	      		
	       			 Elkanah ... an Ephrathite:
	     			And he had two wives; the name of the one was Hannah.... Hannah had conceived, that she
	     			bare a son, and called his name Samuel. 1 Samuel 1:1-2, 20
	     		
	     
	     	And yet Samuel offered sacrfices to God at Mizpeh (away from the tabernacle in Jerusalem) 
	     	and God didn''t seem to mind.     
	     
		        And when the Philistines heard that the children of Israel were gathered 
		        	together to Mizpeh, the lords of the Philistines went up against Israel. And 
		       	 	when the children of Israel heard it, they were afraid of the Philistines.And 
		        	the children of Israel said to Samuel, Cease not to cry unto the LORD our God 
		       		 for us, that he will save us out of the hand of the Philistines. And Samuel 
		        	took a sucking lamb, and offered it for a burnt offering wholly unto the LORD: 
		       		 and Samuel cried unto the LORD for Israel; and the LORD heard him. 1 Samuel 7:7-9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (305, 142, 'Yes, it is necessary.', 'Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy. Exodus 20:8
				    
				    My sabbaths ye shall keep: for it is a sign between me and you throughout your generations ...  
				    for a perpetual covenant. Exodus 31:13-16
				    
				    
Ye shall ... keep my sabbaths: I am the LORD your God. Leviticus 19:3, 
				    30
				    
				    
Six days shall work be done: but the seventh day is the sabbath of rest, an holy convocation; 
				    ye shall do no work therein: it is the sabbath of the LORD. Leviticus 23:3
				
				 
Keep the sabbath day to sanctify it, as the Lord thy God hath
				          commanded thee. Deuteronomy 5:12
				          
				     
 Blessed is the man ... that keepeth the sabbath. Isaiah 56:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (306, 142, 'No, it doesn''t matter at all.', 'The new moons and sabbaths, the calling of assemblies,
				          I cannot away with; it is iniquity. Isaiah 1:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (307, 143, 'Judge not.', 'Jesus commanded his disciples not to judge.
				  
				  
				        Judge not, that ye be not judged. Matthew 7:1
				
				        Judge not, and ye shall not be judged. Luke 6:37
				        

				        
				        And Paul seemed to agree with Jesus on that. (At least in Romans) 
				
				      Therefore thou art inexcusable, O man, whosoever thou art that judgest:
				    for wherein thou judgest another, thou condemnest thyself; for thou that
				    judgest doest the same things. Romans 2:1
				    
				    But why dost thou judge thy brother? or why dost thou set at nought thy brother? 
				    for we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Christ. 
				    Romans 14:10

				    
				    Or until Jesus comes. (In First Corinthians)
				    
				    

				    	Judge nothing before the time, until the Lord come. 1 Corinthians 4:5
				    

				    
				    As did the author of James.
				
				      Who art thou that judgest another? James 4:12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (308, 143, 'Judge everything and everyone.', 'Leviticus says that righteous people should judge others.  
				    
				      

				 In righteousness shalt thou judge thy neighbour. Leviticus 19:15
				 
				 
				 In the gospel of John, Jesus said that we should "judge righteous judgment."
				
				        Judge not according to the appearance, but judge righteous judgment. 
				        John 7:24

				        
				  And Paul said that spiritual people should judge "all things" in this life and will 
				  judge angels in the next.
				
				        
				        				        
				        But he that is spiritual judgeth all things, yet he
				          himself is judged of no man. 1 Corinthians 2:15

				        
I ... have judged already, as though I were present, concerning him that hath so done this deed. 
				        1 Corinthians 5:3
				
				        
For what have I to do to judge them also that are without? do
				          not ye judge them that are within? But them that are without God
				          judgeth. Therefore put away from among yourselves that wicked
				          person. 1 Corinthians 5:12-13
				
				        
Do ye not know that the saints shall judge the world?
				          and if the world shall be judged by you, are ye unworthy to judge the
				          smallest matters? Know ye not that we shall judge angels? how
				          much more things that pertain to this life?. 1 Corinthians 6:2-3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (309, 144, 'Yes, we should hate some people.', 'If any man come to me, and hate not his father, and mother, and wife, and
				     children, and brethren, and sisters, yea, and his own life also, he cannot be
				     my disciple. Luke 14:26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (310, 144, 'No, we should never hate anyone.', 'Thou shalt not hate  thy brother in thine heart. Leviticus 19:17
				      
				      Love thy neighbour as thyself. Leviticus 19:18
				      
				      
Whosoever hateth his brother is a murderer: and ye know that no murderer hath eternal life 
				     abiding in him. 1 John 3:15
				     
				       
If a man say, I love God, and hateth his brother, he is a liar: for he
				     that loveth not his brother whom he hath seen, how can he love God whom he hath 
				     not seen? And this commandment have we from him, That he who loveth
				     God love his brother also. 1 John 4:20-21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (311, 145, 'Kill them.', 'If thy brother, the son of thy mother, or thy son, or thy daughter, or the wife of thy bosom, 
				or thy friend, which is as thine own soul, entice thee secretly, saying, Let us go and serve other 
				gods, which thou hast not known, thou, nor thy fathers; Namely, of the gods of the people which are 
				round about you ... Thou shalt not consent unto him, nor hearken unto him; neither shall thine eye 
				pity him, neither shalt thou spare, neither shalt thou conceal him: But thou shalt
				    surely kill him; thine hand shall be first upon him to put him to death, and
				    afterwards the hand of all the people. And thou shalt stone him with stones, that he die. 
				    Deuteronomy 13:6-10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (312, 145, 'Shun them.', 'Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers: for what fellowship hath righteousness
				    with unrighteousness? and what communion hath light with darkness? And what concord hath
				    Christ with Belial? or what part hath he that believeth with an infidel? ... Wherefore come out
				    from among them, and be ye separate, saith the Lord. 2 Corinthians 6:14-17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (313, 145, 'Love and be kind to them.', 'Love thy neighbor as thyself. Leviticus 19:18, 
				      Matthew 22:39, Mark 12:31, 
				      Luke 10:27, Romans 13:9-10, 
				      Galatians 5:14, James 2:8 
				       
				      Love your enemies. Matthew 5:44, 
				      Luke 6:27
				       
				      
Whatsoever ye would that men should do to you, do ye even so to them. 
				      Matthew 7:12, Luke 6:31', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (314, 146, 'They should be executed.', 'And the man that committeth adultery with another man''s wife, even he that committeth adultery with his neighbour''s wife, the 
				        adulterer and the adulteress shall surely be put to death. Leviticus 20:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (315, 146, 'They should not be punished.', 'And the scribes and Pharisees brought unto him a woman taken in adultery; and when they had set her in the midst, They say unto him,
				         Master, this woman was taken in adultery, in the very act. Now Moses in the law commanded us, that such should be stoned: but what sayest 
				         thou? This they said, tempting him, that they might have to accuse him. But Jesus stooped down, and with his finger wrote on the ground, as 
				         though he heard them not. So when they continued asking him, he lifted up himself, and said unto them, He that is without sin among you, 
				         let him first cast a stone at her. John 8:3-8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (316, 147, 'They should be killed.', 'If a man also lie with
				    mankind, as he lieth with a woman, both of them have committed an
				    abomination: they shall surely be put to death; their blood shall be
				    upon them. Leviticus 20:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (317, 147, 'They should be exiled.', 'And Asa did that which was right in the eyes of the LORD, ... he took away 
				        the sodomites out of the land. 1 Kings 15:11-12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (318, 148, 'He shall be unclean for seven days.', 'And if any man lie with her at all, and her flowers be upon him, he shall be unclean seven days; and all the bed whereon he lieth shall be unclean. Leviticus 15:24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (319, 148, 'He and the woman shall be cut off from among their people.', 'And if a man shall lie with a woman having her sickness, and shall uncover her nakedness; he hath discovered her fountain, and she hath uncovered the fountain of her blood: and both of them shall be cut off from among their people. Leviticus 20:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (320, 149, 'Yes, God is love and he loves everyone.', 'For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should
				     not perish, but have everlasting life. John 3:16
				     
				       He that loveth not knoweth not God; for God is love. 1 John 4:8
				       
				       
And we have known and believed the love that God hath to us. God is love; and he that dwelleth in
				    love dwelleth in God, and God in him. 1 John 4:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (321, 149, 'No, God hates some people.', 'He hates entire nations sometimes.
				    
				     
				        And ye shall not walk in the manners of the nation, which I cast out before you: for they committed all these things,
				     and therefore I abhorred them. Leviticus 20:23

				     
				     
				     He hated Job.
				     
				     
				     He [God] teareth me in his wrath, who hateth me: he gnasheth upon me with his teeth. Job 16:9
				     				     
				         
				      He hates all workers of iniquity.
				
				     Thou hatest all workers of iniquity. Psalm 5:5

				   
				     
				        He hates wicked people and those who love violence.
				        
				       
				       I hated them: for the wickedness of their doings. Hosea 9:15
				       
				        To God the wicked and his wickedness are hateful alike. Wisdom 14:9
				        
				        
The wicked ... whom the Lord abhorreth. Psalm 10:3
				       
				       
The LORD trieth the righteous: but the wicked and him that loveth violence his soul hateth. Psalm 11:5

				       
				       He hates false witnesses and busibodies.
				        
				        These six things doth the LORD hate ... A false witness that speaketh lies, and he that soweth discord 
				        among brethren. Proverbs 6:16, 19

				        
				       He hates people who don''t obey him.
				       
				       
				       But if ye will not hearken unto me, and will not do all these commandments ... my soul shall abhor you. 
				       Leviticus 26:14-30
				       
				       
				       
				       And (for some strange reason) he hates Esau. 
				        
				       And I hated Esau, and laid his mountains and his heritage waste for the dragons of the wilderness. Malachi 1:3
				
				      As it is written, Jacob have I loved, but Esau have I hated. Romans 9:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (322, 150, 'Yes', 'Neither let the eunuch say, Behold, I am a dry tree. For thus saith the LORD unto the eunuchs that keep my sabbaths, and choose the things that please me, and take hold of my covenant; Even unto them will I give in mine house and within my walls a place and a name better than of sons and of daughters: I will give them an everlasting name, that shall not be cut off. Isaiah 56:3-5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (323, 150, 'No', 'Whosoever he be of thy seed in their generations that hath any blemish, let him not approach to offer the bread of his God. For whatsoever man he be that hath a blemish, he shall not approach: a blind man, or a lame, or he that hath a flat nose ... or hath his stones broken; No man that hath a blemish of the seed of Aaron the priest shall come nigh to offer the offerings of the Lord made by fire: he hath a blemish; he shall not come nigh to offer the bread of his God. Leviticus 21:17-21

He that is wounded in the stones, or hath his privy member cut off, shall not enter into the congregation of the LORD. Deuteronomy 23:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (324, 151, 'Yes', 'And if a man cause a blemish in his neighbour; as he hath done, so shall it be done to him; Breach for breach, eye for eye, tooth for tooth: as he hath caused a blemish in a man, so shall it be done to him again. Leviticus 24:19-20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (325, 151, 'No', 'Ye have heard that it hath been said, An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth: But I say unto you, That ye resist not evil: but whosoever shall smite thee on thy right cheek, turn to him the other also. Matthew 5:38-39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (326, 152, 'Yes.', 'God commands us to fear him.
				  
				  
				        Thou shalt fear thy God: for I am the LORD your God. Leviticus 25:17
				        
				        That thou mightest fear the LORD thy God, to keep all his
				          statutes and his commandments. Deuteronomy 6:2
				        
				        
Thou shalt fear the LORD thy God. Deuteronomy 6:13
				        
				         
And the LORD commanded us ... to fear the LORD our God. Deuteronomy 6:24
				
				         
What doth the LORD thy God require of thee, but to
				          fear the LORD thy God. Deuteronomy 10:12
				          
				         
Thou shalt fear the LORD thy God. Deuteronomy 10:20
				         
				        
Fear the Lord. Joshua 24:14, 
				        1 Samuel 12:24, Proverbs 3:7  
				        
				       
Let all the earth fear the LORD. Psalm 33:8
				       
				       
My son, fear thou the LORD. Proverbs 24:21 
				       
				       
God doeth it, that men should fear before him. Ecclesiastes 3:14    
				       
				
For in the multitude of dreams and many words there are also divers vanities: but fear 
				      thou God. Ecclesiastes 5:7 
				      
				
Fear God, and keep his commandments: for this is the whole
				          duty of man. Ecclesiastes 12:13 
				        
				       			
				
Sanctify the LORD of hosts himself; and let him be your fear, and let him
				    be your dread. Isaiah 8:13
				    
				    
Fear ye not me? saith the LORD: will ye not tremble at my presence? Jeremiah 5:22
				    
				    
Fear the Lord and his goodness in the latter days. Hosea 3:5
				    
				    
Having therefore these promises, dearly beloved, let us cleanse
				          ourselves from all filthiness of the flesh and spirit, perfecting
				          holiness in the fear of God. 2 Corinthians 7:1
				          
				     
Submitting yourselves one to another in the fear of God. Ephesians 5:21
				
				
Fear God. 1 Peter 2:17
				
				
Saying with a loud voice, Fear God, and give glory to him;
				          for the hour of his judgment is come. Revelation 14:7
				                  
				        

				        
				        So learn to fear him and teach your children to do likewise.    
				        
				        That they may learn to fear me all the days that they shall live upon 
				        the earth, and that they may teach their children. Deuteronomy 4:10
				        
				        And that their children, which have not known any thing, may hear,
				          and learn to fear the LORD your God. Deuteronomy 31:13
				        
				        
That thou mayest learn to fear the LORD thy God always. Deuteronomy 14:23
				
				 
Gather the people together, men and women, and children, and thy
				          stranger that is within thy gates, that they may hear, and that they
				          may learn, and fear the LORD your God. Deuteronomy 31:12
				
				        
  
				 
				Fear God all day long.
				
				
				    Be thou in the fear of the LORD all the day long. Proverbs 23:17
				            
				          
				   Fear his glorious and fearful name.  
				          
				        
				        That thou mayest fear this glorious and fearful name, THE LORD THY GOD. 
				        Deuteronomy 28:58
				        
				         
				              
				    Fear him above all the other gods.   
				    
				
				       The Lord ... is to be feared above all gods. 1 Chronicles 16:25
				       
				       For the LORD is great, and greatly to be praised: he is to
				          be feared above all gods. Psalm 96:4
				       
   
				           
				       Fear him like Levi did.
				   
				
				That my covenant might be with Levi, saith the LORD of hosts. My covenant was with 
				        him of life and peace; and I gave them to him for the
				    fear wherewith he feared me, and was afraid before my name. Malachi 2:4-5
				      
				
				 And like upright people still do.
				          
				          
				           He that walketh in his uprightness feareth the LORD. Proverbs 14:2
				           
				           
				The whole world should fear him.
				
				
				That all the people of the earth might know the hand of the LORD,
				          that it is mighty: that ye might fear the LORD your God for ever. 
				          Joshua 4:24
				          
				  Who shall not fear thee, O Lord? Revelation 15:4
				
				

				
				But no one does.
				
				
				As it is written, There is none righteous, no, not one: ... There is no 
				        fear of God before their eyes. Romans 3:10-18
				   
				
				Slaves should fear God and obey their masters.
				
				
				Servants, obey in all things your masters according to the flesh; not with eyeservice, as
				    menpleasers; but in singleness of heart, fearing God. Colossians 3:22
				                
				           
				If you fear God, he will help you defeat your enemies.         
				
				        If ye will fear the LORD, and serve him, and obey his voice, and not
				          rebel against the commandment of the LORD, then shall both ye and also
				          the king that reigneth over you continue following the LORD your God. 
				          1 Samuel 12:14             
				
				        But the LORD your God ye shall fear; and he shall deliver you
				          out of the hand of all your enemies. 2 Kings 17:39          
				          

				          
				    And you''ll become rich and famous.
				      
				      
				           By humility and the fear of the LORD are riches, and honour, and life. Proverbs 22:4
				

				
				Nothing bad will ever happen to you.
				
				
				The fear of the LORD ... shall not be visited with evil.  Proverbs 19:23
				
				It shall go well with him that feareth the Lord. Ecclesiasticus 1:19
				

				
				Fearing God makes you live longer.
				     
				The fear of the LORD prolongeth days. Proverbs 10:27
				    
				            
				And is the begining of wisdom and knowledge.
				
				    
				
				     The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom. Proverbs 9:10,
				      Psalm 111:10   
				      
				     
The fear of the LORD is the instruction of wisdom. Proverbs 15:33
				
				     
The fear of the LORD, that is wisdom. Job 28:28
				     
				     
 The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge. Proverbs 1:7
				     
				     
The fear of the Lord is the beginning and crown of wisdom. Ecclesiasticus 1:16
				
				

				
				The fear of the Lord is clean and it endures forever.  
				
				
				      The fear of the LORD is clean, enduring for ever. Psalm 19:9
				      
				      
				      Those who fear the Lord know God''s secret.
				
				      The secret of the LORD is with them that fear him. Psalm 25:14
				      
				      
				     God has his eye on, and takes pleasure from, those that fear him.
				
				      The eye of the LORD is upon them that fear him. Psalm 33:18
				      
				      The LORD taketh pleasure in them that fear him. Psalm 147:11
				             

				            
				 And he will satisfy all of their desires.
				      
				      He will fulfil the desire of them that fear him. 
				      Psalm 145:19
				      
				       The fear of the LORD ... he that hath it shall abide satisfied. 
				      Proverbs 19:23
				
      
				      
				      People that fear God have whatever they want.
				
				      O fear the LORD, ye his saints: for there is no want to them that fear him. 
				      Psalm 34:9
				           
				          
				      God has mercy on those that fear him. 
				
				        Great is his mercy toward them that fear him.  
				        Psalm 103:11 
				        
				        But the mercy of the LORD is from everlasting to everlasting upon them
				    that fear him. Psalm 103:17
				    
				    
And his mercy is on them that fear him from generation to
				          generation. Luke 1:50
				        

				        
				Blesses them.
				 
				        Blessed is the man that feareth the LORD. Psalm 112:1 
				        
				        He will bless them that fear the LORD. Psalm 115:13
				        
				        
Blessed is every one that feareth the LORD. Psalm 128:1
				        
				        
        
				          
				 Pities them.    
				
				        The LORD pitieth them that fear him. Psalm 103:13 
				           
				        
				And saves them.
				
				 He ... will hear their cry, and will save them.   Psalm 145:19
				 
				
				
				If you fear God''s name, the Sun of righteousness will heal you with his wings, and you''ll grow up like a 
				calf in a stall.
				
				But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; 
				and ye shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall. Malachi 4:2
				
				       
				 Fear God since he is able to destroy your soul and body in hell.   
				            
				        Fear him which is able to destroy both soul and body in hell. 
				        Matthew 10:28, Luke 12:5
				        
				
				   It is a fearful thing to fall into God''s hands.
				   
				
				     It is a fearful thing to fall into the hands of the living God. 
				     Hebrews 10:31', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (327, 152, 'No.', 'God has given believers the spirit of love, not of fear.
				    
				      
				        For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power,
				          and of love, and of a sound mind. 2 Timothy 1:7

				          
				          Not as fearful slaves, but as the children of a loving God.
				          
				          For ye have not received the spirit of bondage again to fear; but ye have received 
				          the Spirit of adoption, whereby we cry, Abba, Father. Romans 8:15

				          
				      God is love, and there is no fear in love.    
				          
				        
				        God is Love. 1 John 4:8
				        
				        There is no fear in love; but perfect love casteth out
				          fear: because fear hath torment. He that feareth is not made
				          perfect in love. 1 John 4:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (328, 153, 'Yes', 'And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, saying,

					Number the children of Levi after the house of their fathers, by their families: 
					every male from a month old and upward shalt thou number them. Numbers 3:14-15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (329, 153, 'No', 'The LORD had spoken unto Moses, saying, 
				Only thou shalt not number the tribe of Levi, neither take the sum of them among the children of Israel.
				 Numbers 1:48-49
				 
				 
				  But the Levites were not numbered among the children of Israel; as the LORD commanded Moses. 
				 Numbers 2:33', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (330, 154, '22,000', 'All that were numbered of the Levites, which Moses and Aaron numbered at the commandment of the LORD, throughout their families, all the males from a month old and upward, were twenty and two thousand. Numbers 3:39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (331, 154, '22,300', 'The sons of Levi by their names; Gershon, and Kohath, and Merari. Numbers 3:17

There were 7,500 male Gersonites.

Of Gershon was the family of the Libnites, and the family of the Shimites: these are the families of the Gershonites.

Those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, even those that were numbered of them were seven thousand and five hundred. Numbers 3:21-22



There were 8,600 male Kohathites.


And of Kohath was the family of the Amramites, and the family of the Izeharites, and the family of the Hebronites, and the family of the Uzzielites: these are the families of the Kohathites.

In the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, were eight thousand and six hundred. Numbers 3:27-28


 There were 6,200 male Merariites.

Of Merari was the family of the Mahlites, and the family of the Mushites: these are the families of Merari.

And those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, were six thousand and two hundred. Numbers 3:33-34

For a total of 22,300 male Levites.', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (332, 155, '20 years old', 'The priests and the Levites, and all they that were come out of the captivity 
				unto Jerusalem; and appointed the Levites, from twenty years old and upward. Ezra 3:8
				
				
These were the sons of Levi ... as they were counted ... from the age of twenty years and upward. 
				1 Chronicles 23:24 
				
				
 For by the last words of David the Levites were numbered from twenty years old and above. 
				1 Chronicles 23:27
				
				
Both to the genealogy of the priests by the house of their fathers, and the Levites from twenty years old and upward. 
				2 Chronicles 31:17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (333, 155, '25 years old', 'The Levites: from twenty and five years old and upward they shall go in to wait upon the service of the tabernacle 
				of the congregation. Numbers 8:24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (334, 155, '30 years old', 'From thirty years old and upward even until fifty years old, all that enter into the host, 
					to do the work in the tabernacle of the congregation. Numbers 4:3			
				
				 Now the Levites were numbered from the age of thirty years and upward. 1 Chronicles 23:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (335, 156, 'Long hair on men is encouraged.', 'No razor shall come upon his [a Nazarite''s] head. He shall be
          holy, and shall let the locks of the hair on his head grow. Numbers 6:5
          
        For, lo, thou shalt conceive, and bear a son [Samson]; and no
          razor shall come on his head: for the child shall be a
          Nazarite. Judges 13:5
          
        
I will give him [Samuel] unto the Lord all the days of his
          life, and there shall no razor come upon his head. 1 Samuel 1:11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (336, 156, 'Long hair on men is shameful.', 'Doth not even nature herself teach you, that, if a man have
	          long hair, it is a shame unto him? 1 Corinthians 11:14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (337, 156, 'Priests may not have long hair.', 'The priests ... shall not .... sufer their locks to grow long. Ezekiel 44:15-20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (338, 157, 'Moses wrote the entire Pentateuch.', 'And Moses wrote this law, and delivered it unto the priests the sons of Levi. Deuteronomy 31:9
				        
				        These be the words which Moses spake unto all Israel on this side Jordan
				    in the wilderness. Deuteronomy 1:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (339, 157, 'There were other authors.', 'Now the man Moses was
				    very meek, above all the men which were upon the face of the earth. Numbers 12:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (340, 158, 'Only Caleb', 'And Caleb stilled the people before Moses, and said, Let us go up at once, and possess it; for we are well able to overcome it. 
				Numbers 13:30', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (341, 158, 'Both Caleb and Joshua', 'And Joshua the son of Nun, and Caleb the son of Jephunneh, which were of them that searched the land, 
				rent their clothes: And they spake unto all the company of the children of Israel, saying, The land, which we 
				passed through to search it, is an exceeding good land. If the LORD delight in us, then he will bring us into this 
				land, and give it us; a land which floweth with milk and honey. Only rebel not ye against the LORD, neither fear 
				ye the people of the land; for they are bread for us: their defence is departed from them, and the LORD is with us: 
				fear them not. Numbers 14:6-9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (342, 159, 'We should follow our heart and eyes.', 'Walk in the ways of thine heart, and in the sight of thine
				          eyes. Ecclesiastes 11:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (343, 159, 'We should not follow our heart and eyes.', 'Seek not after your own heart and your own eyes. Numbers 15:39
				        
				        He that trusteth in his own heart is a fool. Proverbs 28:26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (344, 160, 'That he struck the rock instead of talking to it.', 'And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying, Take the rod, and gather thou the assembly together, thou, and Aaron thy brother, and speak ye unto the rock before their eyes; and it shall give forth his water, and thou shalt bring forth to them water out of the rock....

And Moses lifted up his hand, and with his rod he smote the rock twice: and the water came out...

And the LORD spake unto Moses and Aaron, Because ye believed me not, to sanctify me in the eyes of the children of Israel, therefore ye shall not bring this congregation into the land which I have given them. Numbers 20:7-12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (345, 160, 'God was angry with the people.', 'The LORD was wroth with me for your sakes, and would not hear me: and the LORD said unto me, ... Get thee up into the top of Pisgah, and lift up thine eyes westward, and northward, and southward, and eastward, and behold it with thine eyes: for thou shalt not go over this Jordan. Deuteronomy 3:26-27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (346, 161, 'Aaron died on mount Hor.', 'And Moses did as the LORD commanded: and they went up into mount
				          Hor in the sight of all the congregation. And Moses stripped Aaron
				          of his garments, and put them upon Eleazar his son; and Aaron died
				          there in the top of the mount. Numbers 20:27-28
				
				        And Aaron the priest went up into mount Hor at the
				          commandment of the LORD, and died there. Numbers 33:38', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (347, 161, 'Aaron died at Mosera.', 'And the children of Israel took their journey from Beeroth of
				          the children of Jaakan to Mosera: there Aaron died, and there
				          he was buried. Deuteronomy 10:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (348, 162, 'Yes', 'An Ammonite or Moabite shall not enter into the congregation of the LORD; even to their tenth generation shall 
				they not enter into the congregation of the LORD for ever ... because they hired against thee Balaam the son of Beor of 
				Pethor of Mesopotamia, to curse thee. Deuteronomy 23:3-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (349, 162, 'No', 'Balak the king of Moab hath brought me from Aram, out of the mountains of the east, saying, Come, curse me Jacob, 
				and come, defy Israel. How shall I curse, whom God hath not cursed? or how shall I defy, whom the LORD hath not 
				defied? Numbers 23:7-8

				
Balak''s anger was kindled against Balaam, and he smote his hands together: and Balak said unto Balaam, I called 
				thee to curse mine enemies, and, behold, thou hast altogether blessed them these three times. 
				Numbers 24:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (350, 163, 'No, God cannot and does not lie.', 'God is not a man, that he should lie; neither the son of man, that he should repent. Numbers 23:19

The Strength of Israel will not lie nor repent. 1 Samuel 15:29

Thou art that God, and thy words be true. 2 Samuel 7:28

Thy word is true from the beginning. Psalm 119:160

In hope of eternal life, which God, that cannot lie, promised before the world began. Titus 1:2

It was impossible for God to lie. Hebrews 6:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (351, 163, 'Yes, God lies by proxy; He sends prophets or lying spirits to deceive.', 'Now, therefore, behold, the Lord hath put a lying spirit in the mouth of these thy prophets, and the Lord hath spoken evil concerning thee. 1 Kings 22:23

Now therefore, behold, the Lord hath put a lying spirit in the mouth of these thy prophets. 2 Chronicles 18:22

Ah, Lord GOD! surely thou hast greatly deceived this people. Jeremiah 4:10

O Lord, thou hast deceived me, and I was deceived. Jeremiah 20:7

And if a prophet be deceived when he hath spoken a thing, I the Lord have deceived that prophet. Ezekiel 14:9

For this cause God shall send them strong delusion, that they should believe a lie. 2 Thessalonians 2:11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (352, 164, '23,000.', 'Neither let us commit fornication, as some of them committed, and fell in one day three and twenty thousand. 1 Corinthians 10:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (353, 164, '24,000.', 'And those that died in the plague were twenty and four thousand. Numbers 25:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (354, 165, 'Yes, God buried them alive.', 'So they gat up from the tabernacle of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram ... and stood in the door of their tents, 
				        and their wives, and their sons, and their little children.... And the earth opened her mouth, and swallowed them up, and their houses, 
				        and all the men that appertained unto Korah, and all their goods. They, and all that appertained to them, went down alive into the pit, 
				        and the earth closed upon them: and they perished from among the congregation. Numbers 16:27-33', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (355, 165, 'No, some of them survived.', 'Notwithstanding the children of Korah died not. Numbers 26:11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (356, 166, 'Hepher', 'Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh. Numbers 27:1, Joshua 17:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (357, 166, 'Manasseh', 'The sons of Manasseh; Ashriel ... and the name of the second was Zelophehad. 1 Chronicles 7:14-15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (358, 167, 'Two bullocks, one ram, seven lambs, and a goat.', 'And in the beginnings
				    of your months ye shall offer a burnt offering unto the LORD; two young
				    bullocks, and one ram, seven lambs of the first year without spot ... 
				    And one kid of the goats for a sin offering unto the LORD shall be offered, 
				    beside the continual burnt offering Numbers 28:11-15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (359, 167, 'One bullock, one ram, and six lambs.', 'And in the day of the new moon it shall be a young bullock without
				    blemish, and six lambs, and a ram. Ezekiel 46:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (360, 168, 'Yes.', 'And they warred against the Midianites, as the LORD commanded Moses; and they slew all 
				        the males. 
				        ...
				       Now therefore kill every male among the little ones, and kill every woman that hath known man
				    by lying with him. But all the women children, that have not known a man by lying with him, keep 
				    alive for yourselves. Numbers 31:7, 16-17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (361, 168, 'No.', 'And the children of Israel did evil in the sight of the LORD: and the LORD delivered them 
				        into the hand of Midian seven years. And the hand of Midian prevailed against Israel. 
				        ...
				    For they came up with their cattle and their tents, and they came as grasshoppers for 
				    multitude; for both they and their camels were without number. Judges 6:1-2, 5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (362, 169, 'Yes, he was the meekest man who ever lived.', 'Now the man Moses was very meek, above all the men which were upon the face of the earth. Numbers 12:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (363, 169, 'No, he was vicious and cruel.', 'And Moses was wroth with the officers.... And Moses said unto them, Have ye saved
				    all the women alive? ... Now therefore kill every male among the little ones, and kill every 
				    woman that hath known man by lying with him. But all the women children, that have not known a 
				    man by lying with him, keep alive for yourselves. Numbers 31:14-18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (364, 170, 'Only Caleb', 'Because all those men which have seen my glory, and my miracles, which I did in Egypt and in the wilderness, 
				and have tempted me now these ten times, and have not hearkened to my voice; Surely they shall not see the land which I 
				sware unto their fathers, neither shall any of them that provoked me see it: But my servant Caleb, because he had another spirit with him, 
				and hath followed me fully, him will I bring into the land whereinto he went; and his seed shall possess it. 
				Numbers 14:22-24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (365, 170, 'Both Caleb and Joshua', 'Even those men that did bring up the evil report upon the land, died by the plague before the LORD. 
				But Joshua the son of Nun, and Caleb the son of Jephunneh, which were of the men that went to search the land, lived still. 
				 Numbers 14:37-38

				
But among these there was not a man of them whom Moses and Aaron the priest numbered, 
				when they numbered the children of Israel in the wilderness of Sinai. 
				For the LORD had said of them, They shall surely die in the wilderness. And there was not left a man of them, 
				save Caleb the son of Jephunneh and Joshua the son of Nun. Numbers 26:64-65				
				
				
And the LORD''s anger was kindled the same time, and he sware, saying, Surely none of the men that came up out of Egypt, from 
				twenty years old and upward, shall see the land which I sware unto Abraham, unto Isaac, and unto Jacob; because they have not 
				wholly followed me:  Save Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite, and Joshua the son of Nun: for they have wholly followed the 
				LORD. Numbers 32:10-12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (366, 171, 'God doesn''t get angry.', 'God will not threaten like man, nor be inflamed to anger. Judith 8:15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (367, 171, 'God''s anger lasts for just a moment.', 'For his anger endureth but a moment. Psalm 30:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (368, 171, 'God''s anger lasts a long time.', 'And the Lord''s anger was kindled against Israel, and he made
				          them wander in the wilderness for forty years. Numbers 32:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (369, 171, 'God''s anger doesn''t last forever.', 'Neither will he keep his anger for ever. Psalm 103:9
				        
				        
I am merciful, saith the Lord, and I will not keep anger for ever. Jeremiah 3:12
				
				        
He retaineth not his anger forever, because he delighteth in  mercy. Micah 7:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (370, 171, 'God''s anger lasts forever.', 'Ye have kindled a fire in mine anger, which shall burn for ever. Jeremiah 17:4
				
				          The people against whom the LORD hath indignation for ever. Malachi 1:4
				          
				         
Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels. Matthew 25:41
				
				         
And these shall go away into everlasting punishment. Matthew 25:46', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (371, 172, 'Do not fight against them or take their land.', 'And the LORD said unto me [Moses], Distress not the Moabites, neither contend with them 
				  in battle: for I will not give thee of their land for a possession; because I have
				    given Ar unto the children of Lot for a possession. Deuteronomy 2:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (372, 172, 'Kill them and take their land.', 'And he said unto them, Follow after me: for the LORD hath delivered your enemies the
				    Moabites into your hand..... And they slew of Moab
				    at that time about ten thousand men ... and
				    there escaped not a man. Moab was subdued that day under the hand of Israel. Judges 3:28-30
				    
				    There shall be no more praise of Moab. ... Come, and let us cut it off from being a nation. Jeremiah 48:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (373, 173, 'Do not fight against them or take their land.', 'And when thou comest
				    nigh over against the children of Ammon, distress them not, nor meddle with
				    them: for I will not give thee of the land of the children of Ammon any
				    possession; because I have given it unto the children of Lot for a
				    possession. Deuteronomy 2:19
				    
				    Only unto the land of the children of Ammon thou camest not ... nor unto
				    whatsoever the LORD our God forbad us. Deuteronomy 2:37
				     
(However, we avoided the land of the Ammonites all along the Jabbok River and the towns 
				     in the hill countryall the places the LORD our God had commanded us to leave alone. v.37 from the New Living Translation)', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (374, 173, 'Kill them and take their land.', 'So Jephthah passed over unto the children of Ammon to fight against them; and the LORD 
				        delivered them into his hands. Judges 11:32
				
				    I will cause an alarm of war to be heard in Rabbah of the Ammonites; and it shall be a 
				    desolate heap, and her daughters shall be burned with fire. Jeremiah 49:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (375, 174, 'The earth will last forever.', 'That thou mayest prolong thy days upon the earth, which the
				          Lord thy God giveth thee for ever. Deuteronomy 4:40
				          
				      The righteous shall inherit the land, and dwell therein for ever. Psalm 37:29
				      
				        
The earth which he hath established for ever. Psalm 78:69
				        
				        
Who laid the foundations of the earth, that it should
				          not be removed for ever. Psalm 104:5
				          
				        
One generation passeth away, and another generation cometh:
				          but the earth abideth for ever. Ecclessiastes 1:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (376, 174, 'The earth will not last forever, but will be destroyed.', 'The earth and the heavens are the work of thy hands.
				          They shall perish. Psalm 102:25-26
				 
				        For, behold, I create a new heavens and a new earth. Isaiah 65:17
				        
				                  
				        
Heaven and earth shall pass away; but my words shall
				          not pass away. Matthew 24:35, Mark 13:31,
				          Luke 21:33
				          
				        
Thou, Lord, in the beginning hast laid the foundation of the
				          earth; and the heavens are the works of thine hands. They shall
				          perish. Hebrews 1:10-11
				          
				        
The heavens shall pass away with a great noise, and the
				          elements shall melt with fervent heat, the earth also and the
				          works that are therein shall be burned up. 2 Peter 3:10 
				          
				        
Nevertheless we, according to his promise, look for new
				          heavens and a new earth. 2 Peter 3:13
				          
				      
And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and
				     the first earth were passed away. Revelation 21:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (377, 175, 'Yes, they saw him face to face.', 'The LORD our God made a covenant with us in Horeb ... The LORD talked with you face to face 
				  in the mount out of the midst of the fire. Deuteronomy 5:2-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (378, 175, 'No, they only heard a voice.', 'The LORD spake unto you out of the midst of the fire: ye heard the voice of the words, but saw no similitude; 
				      only ye heard a voice. Deuteronomy 4:12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (379, 176, 'Yes, they are binding forever.', 'Know therefore that the LORD thy God, he is God, the faithful God, which keepeth covenant and mercy with them that love him and keep his commandments to a thousand generations. Deuteronomy 7:9

Therefore thou shalt love the LORD thy God, and keep his charge, and his statutes, and his judgments, and his commandments, alway. Deuteronomy 11:1

These are the statutes and judgments, which ye shall observe ... all the days that ye live upon the earth. Deuteronomy 12:1

Be ye mindful always of his covenant; the word which he commanded to a thousand generations ... an everlasting covenant. 1 Chronicles 16:15

Thou art near, O LORD; and all thy commandments are truth. Concerning thy testimonies, I have known of old that thou hast founded them for ever. Psalm 119:151-2

Thy word is true from the beginning: and every one of thy righteous judgments endureth for ever. Psalm 119:160', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (380, 176, 'No, there are only two laws that you must obey.', 'Jesus said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind.
This is the first and great commandment.

And the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.

On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets. Matthew 22:37-40', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (381, 176, 'No, they were only temporary.', 'The law and the prophets were until John [the Baptist]: since that time the kingdom of heaven is preached. Luke 16:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (382, 177, 'Yes.', 'And they prayed, and said, Thou, Lord, which knowest the
			          hearts of all men. Acts 1:24
			          
			        He knoweth the secrets of the heart. Psalm 44:21
			        
			        
Thou knowest my down-sitting and mine up-rising; thou
			          understands my thought afar off. Thou compassest my path and my lying
			          down, and art acquainted with all my ways. Psalm 139:2-3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (383, 177, 'No.', 'And thou shalt remember all the way which the LORD thy God led thee these
			    forty years in the wilderness, to humble thee, and to prove thee, to know what was in thine
			    heart, whether thou wouldest keep his commandments, or no. Deuteronomy 8:2
			    
			        For the Lord your God proveth you, to know whether ye
			          love the Lord your God with all your soul. Deuteronomy 13:3
			          
			        
God left him [Hezekiah], to try him, that he might know
			          all that was in his heart. 2 Chronicles 32:31', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (384, 178, 'Yes.', 'Ye are the children of the LORD your God. Deuteronomy 14:1
			        
			        All of you are children of the most High. Psalm 82:6
			        
			        
Ye are the sons of the living God. Hosea 1:10
			        
			        
Be ye therefore perfect, even as your Father which is in heaven is perfect. Matthew 5:48
			        
			        
Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name. Matthew 6:9, 
			        Luke 11:2
			        
			        
Jesus saith unto her, Touch me not; for I am not yet ascended to my Father: but go to my brethren, and say unto them, 
			        I ascend unto my Father, and your Father; and to my God, and your God. John 20:17
			        
			        
We are the offspring of God. Acts 17:29', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (385, 178, 'No.', 'Ye are all the children of God by faith in Christ Jesus. Galatians 3:26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (386, 179, 'Yes.', 'When thou shalt besiege a city a long time, in making war against it to take it, thou shalt not destroy the trees. Deuteronomy 20:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (387, 179, 'No.', 'And ye shall smite every fenced city, and every choice city, and shall fell every good tree. 2 Kings 3:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (388, 180, 'Yes', 'For there are some eunuchs, which were so born from their mother''s womb: and there are some eunuchs, 
        which were made eunuchs of men: and there be eunuchs, 
        which have made themselves eunuchs for the kingdom of heaven''s sake. He that is able to receive it, let him receive it. 
        Matthew 19:12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (389, 180, 'No', 'He that is wounded in the stones, or hath his privy member cut off, shall not enter into the congregation of the LORD. 
				Deuteronomy 23:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (390, 181, 'At least ten.', 'A bastard shall not enter into the congregation of the LORD; even to his tenth generation. Deuteronomy 23:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (391, 181, 'Less than ten.', 'Judas begat Phares ...
Phares ... [Phares was a "bastard" to God. (See Genesis 38:)]
[1] Esrom ...
[2] Aram ...
[3] Aminadab ...
[4] Naasson ...
[5] Salmon ...
[6] Booz ...
[7] Obed ...
[8] Jesse ....
[9] David. Matthew 1:3-5

(See also Luke 3:31-33)', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (392, 182, 'No.', 'An Ammonite or Moabite
				    shall not enter into the congregation of the LORD; even to their tenth
				    generation shall they not enter into the congregation of the LORD for
				    ever. Deuteronomy 23:3
				    
				  On that day they read in the 
				book of Moses in the audience of the people; and therein was found written, that 
				the Ammonite and the Moabite should not come into the congregation of God for 
				ever. Nehemiah 13:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (393, 182, 'Yes.', 'And they took them wives
				    of the women of Moab; the name of the one was Orpah, and the name of
				    the other Ruth. Ruth 1:4
				    
				     So Boaz took Ruth, and she was his wife: and when he went in unto her, the LORD gave her
				    conception, and she bare a son. ... and they called his name Obed: he is the father of Jesse, 
				    the father of David. Ruth 4:13-17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (394, 183, 'Be nice to them.', 'Thou shalt not abhor an Edomite; for he is thy brother. Deuteronomy 23:7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (395, 183, 'Kill them.', 'And he [Amaziah] did that which was right in the sight of the LORD.... He slew of Edom 
			        in the valley of salt ten thousand. 2 Kings 14:3, 7
			        
			        I will also stretch out mine hand upon Edom, and will cut
			    off man and beast from it. Ezekiel 25:13
			    
			        
Thus saith the Lord GOD concerning Edom.... Arise ye, and let us rise 
			        up against her in battle. Obadiah 1
			        
			        
Shall I not in that day, saith the LORD, even destroy the wise men out
			     of Edom, and understanding out of the mount of Esau? ...  that every one of the mount of Esau may be cut off by slaughter. 
			     Obadiah  8-9
			     (According to the Bible, Edomites are the descendants of Esau.)', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (396, 184, 'Yes, it''s always permited.', 'When a man hath taken a wife, and married her, and it come to pass that
				she find no favour in his eyes, because he hath found some uncleanness in
				her: then let him write her a bill of divorcement, and give it in her hand,
				and send her out of his house. And when she is departed out of his house, she may go and be another man''s wife. 
				Deuteronomy 24:1-2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (397, 184, 'Except when the divorced woman remarries the man who divorced her. (That''s an abomination.)', 'And if the latter husband hate her, and write her a bill of divorcement, and giveth it in her hand, 
				    and sendeth her out of his house; or if the latter husband die, which took her to be his wife; Her former husband, 
				    which sent her away, may not take her again to be his wife, after that she is defiled; for that is abomination before the LORD. 
				    Deuteronomy 24:1-2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (398, 184, 'No, it is never permitted.', 'Whosoever putteth away his wife, and marrieth another, committeth adultery: and whosoever marrieth her 
				        that is put away from her husband committeth adultery. Luke 16:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (399, 185, 'Those who follow the law are cursed.', 'For as many as are of the works of the law are under the
				          curse. Galatians 3:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (400, 185, 'Those who do not follow the law are cursed.', 'Cursed be he that confirmeth not all the words of this law to
				          do them. 
				          Deuteronomy 27:26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (401, 186, 'Yes', 'And it will come about that, just as the LORD rejoiced over you to be good to you, and make you numerous, so will the LORD rejoice over you to wipe you out and destroy you; and you will be torn away from the land which you are entering to possess. Deuteronomy 28:63', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (402, 186, 'No', 'Have I any pleasure at all that the wicked should die? saith the Lord GOD: and not that he should return from his ways, and live? Ezekiel 18:23', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (403, 187, 'Yes.', 'I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life. Deuteronomy 30:19

Choose you this day whom ye will serve.... But as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD. Joshua 24:15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (404, 187, 'No.', 'O LORD, I know that the way of man is not in himself: it is not in man that walketh to direct his steps. Jeremiah 10:23

And as many as were ordained to eternal life believed. Acts 13:48

For whom he did foreknow, he also did predestinate.... Moreover whom he did predestinate, them he also called: and whom he called, them he also justified: and whom he justified, them he also glorified. Romans 8:29-30

For the children being not yet born, neither having done any good or evil, that the purpose of God according to election might stand, not of works, but of him that calleth. .... For he saith to Moses, I will have mercy on whom I will have mercy, and I will have compassion on whom I will have compassion. So then it is not of him that willeth, nor of him that runneth, but of God that sheweth mercy. For the scripture saith unto Pharaoh, Even for this same purpose have I raised thee up, that I might shew my power in thee, and that my name might be declared throughout all the earth. Therefore hath he mercy on whom he will have mercy, and whom he will he hardeneth. Thou wilt say then unto me, Why doth he yet find fault? ... Shall the thing formed say to him that formed it, Why hast thou made me thus? Hath not the potter power over the clay, of the same lump to make one vessel unto honour, and another unto dishonour? What if God, willing to shew his wrath, and to make his power known, endured with much longsuffering the vessels of wrath fitted to destruction. Romans 9:11-22

He hath chosen us in him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blame before him in love: Having predestinated us unto the adoption of children by Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will. Ephesians 1:4-5

God shall send them strong delusion, that they should believe a lie: That they all might be damned. 2 Thessalonians 2:11-12

Who hath saved us, and called us with an holy calling, not according to our works, but according to his own purpose and grace, which was given us in Christ Jesus before the world began. 2 Timothy 1:9

For there are certain men crept in unawares, who were before of old ordained to this condemnation. Jude 4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (405, 188, 'Yes', 'And Moses was an hundred and twenty years old when he died: his eye was not dim, nor his natural force abated.
				        Deuteronomy 34:7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (406, 188, 'No', 'And he said unto them, I am an hundred and twenty years old this day; 
				        I can no more go out and come in: also the LORD hath said unto me, Thou shalt not go over this Jordan.
				        Deuteronomy 31:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (407, 189, 'Yes, he asked him directly.', 'And when Jesus was entered into Capernaum, there came unto
				          him a centurion, beseeching him, And saying, Lord, my servant
				          lieth at home sick of the palsy, grievously tormented. And Jesus saith
				          unto him, I will come and heal him. The centurion answered and said, Lord, I am not worthy that
				          thou shouldest come under my roof: but speak the word only, and my
				          servant shall be healed. Matthew 8:5-8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (408, 189, 'No, he sent others to ask for him.', 'He entered into Capernaum. And a certain centurion''s servant,
				          who was dear unto him, was sick, and ready to die. And when he heard
				          of Jesus, he sent unto him the elders of the Jews, beseeching him
				          that he would come and heal his servant. And when they came to
				          Jesus, they besought him.... Then Jesus went with them. ...
				          
				          And when he was now not far from the house, the centurion sent
				          friends to him, saying unto him, Lord, trouble not thyself: for I
				          am not worthy that thou shouldest enter under my roof: Wherefore
				          neither thought I myself worthy to come unto thee: but say in a word,
				          and my servant shall be healed. Luke 7:1-7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (409, 190, 'God', 'For the LORD your God, he is God in heaven above, and in earth beneath. Joshua 2:11
				        
				        The LORD of all the earth Joshua 3:13
				        
				        
Thou art the God, even thou alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth. 2 Kings 19:15
				
				        
He is the LORD our God; his judgments are in all the earth. 1 Chronicles 16:14
				
				        
Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth rejoice: and let men say among the nations, The LORD reigneth. 
				        1 Chronicles 16:31
				        
				        
We are the servants of the God of heaven and earth. Ezra 5:11
				
				        
Who hath given him a charge over the earth? or who hath disposed the whole world? Job 34:13
				        
				        
For the LORD most high is terrible; he is a great King over all the earth. Psalm 47:2
				        
				        
For God is the King of all the earth. Psalm 47:7
				
				        
God ruleth in Jacob unto the ends of the earth. Psalm 59:13
				        
				        
That men may know that thou, whose name alone is JEHOVAH, art the most high over all the earth. Psalm 83:18
				
				        
Say among the heathen that the LORD reigneth. Psalm 96:10 
				        
				        
The LORD reigneth; let the earth rejoice. Psalm 97:1
				        
				        
The hills melted like wax at the presence of the LORD, at the presence of the Lord of the whole earth. Psalm 97:5
				
				        
The LORD reigneth; let the people tremble. Psalm 99:1
				        
				        
His kingdom ruleth over all. Psalm 103:19
				        
				        
Thou art the God, even thou alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth. Isaiah 37:16
				        
				        
The God of the whole earth shall he be called. Isaiah 54:5
				
				        
I will consecrate their gain unto the LORD, and their substance unto the Lord of the whole earth. Micah 4:13 
				        
				        
These are the two anointed ones, that stand by the LORD of the whole earth. Zechariah 4:14
				        
				        
These are the four spirits of the heavens, which go forth from standing before the LORD of all the earth. 
				        Zechariah 6:5
				
				        
Jesus answered and said, I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth. Matthew 11:25
				        
				        
Jesus rejoiced in spirit, and said, I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth. Luke 10:21
				        
				        
God that made the world and all things therein, seeing that he is Lord of heaven and earth. Acts 17:24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (410, 190, 'The Devil (or someone else who isn''t God)', 'The devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain, and sheweth him all the kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them; 
				        And saith unto him, All these things will I give thee. Matthew 4:8-9
				                
				        
				        And the devil, taking him up into an high mountain, shewed unto him all the kingdoms of the world  in a moment of time. 
				        And the devil said unto him, All this power will I give thee. Luke 4:5-7
				        
				        
Now is the judgment of this world: now shall the prince of this world be cast out. John 12:31
				
				        
Hereafter I will not talk much with you: for the prince of this world cometh. John 14:30
				        
				        
Of judgment, because the prince of this world is judged. John 16:11
				        
				        
The god of this world hath blinded the minds of them which believe not. 2 Corinthians 4:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (411, 191, 'Yes, he took them to Gilgal.', 'And those twelve stones, which they took out of Jordan, did Joshua pitch in Gilgal. Joshua 4:20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (412, 191, 'No, they are still there.', 'And Joshua set up twelve stones in the midst of Jordan, in the place where the feet of the priests which bare the ark of the 
				        covenant stood: and they are there unto this day. Joshua 4:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (413, 192, 'No, it was never rebuilt after Joshua destroyed it.', 'And Joshua burnt Ai, and made it an heap for ever, even a desolation unto this day. Joshua 8:28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (414, 192, 'Yes, it existed at the time of the Babylonian captivity.', 'The men of Bethel and Ai, an hundred twenty and three. Nehemiah 7:32', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (415, 194, 'Yes', 'Then Horam king of Gezer came up to help Lachish; and Joshua smote him and his people, 
				until he had left him none remaining. Joshua 10:33', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (416, 194, 'No, they were still there a little later.', 'Neither did Ephraim drive out the Canaanites that dwelt in Gezer; but the Canaanites dwelt in Gezer among them. 
				Judges 1:29:', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (417, 195, 'He was killed by Joshua.', 'And it came to pass, when Jabin king of Hazor had heard those things, 
		        that he sent to Jobab king of Madon, and to the king of Shimron, and to the king of Achshaph, ... Joshua 11:1
		        
		        And Joshua at that time turned back, and took Hazor, and smote the king thereof with the sword: 
		        for Hazor beforetime was the head of all those kingdoms. And they smote all the souls that were therein with the edge of the sword, 
		        utterly destroying them: there was not any left to breathe: and he burnt Hazor with fire.  
		        Joshua 11:10-11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (418, 195, 'He was killed 120 years after Joshua''s death.', 'Now after the death of Joshua it came to pass, that the children of Israel asked the LORD, 
		        saying, Who shall go up for us against the Canaanites first, to fight against them? Judges 1:1
		        
		        And the land had rest forty years. And Othniel the son of Kenaz died. Judges 3:11
		        
		        So Moab was subdued that 
		        day under the hand of Israel. And the land had rest fourscore years. Judges 3:30
		        
		        And the LORD sold them into the hand of Jabin king of Canaan, that reigned in Hazor; the captain of whose host was Sisera, 
		        which dwelt in Harosheth of the Gentiles. Judges 4:2
		        
		        And the hand of the children of Israel prospered, 
		        and prevailed against Jabin the king of Canaan, until they had destroyed Jabin king of Canaan. 
		        Judges 4:24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (419, 196, 'Joshua', 'And at that time came Joshua, and cut off the Anakims from the mountains, from Hebron, 
				        from Debir, from Anab, and from all the mountains of Judah, 
				        and from all the mountains of Israel: Joshua destroyed them utterly with their cities. 
				        Joshua 11:21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (420, 196, 'Caleb', 'And unto Caleb the son of Jephunneh he gave a part among the children of Judah, according to the 
				        commandment of the LORD to Joshua, even the city of Arba the father of Anak, which city is Hebron. 
				        And Caleb drove thence the three sons of Anak, Sheshai, and Ahiman, and Talmai, the children of Anak. 
				        Joshua 15:13-14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (421, 197, 'They were given to Judah.', 'This is the inheritance of the tribe of the children of Judah
				          ... And in the valley, Eshataol and Zoreah. Joshua 15:20, 33', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (422, 197, 'They were given to Dan.', 'And the seventh lot came out for the tribe of the children of Dan
				          according to their families. And the coast of their inheritance was
				          Zorah, and Eshtaol. Joshua 19:40-41', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (423, 198, 'Dan.', 'And out of the tribe of Dan ... Aijalon with her
				          suburbs, Gathrimmon with her suburbs. Joshua 21:23-24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (424, 198, 'Ephraim.', 'The tribe of Ephraim ... Aijalon with her suburbs, and
				          Gathrimmon with her suburbs. 1 Chronicles 6:66, 69', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (425, 199, 'Achan''s father was Carmi.', 'For Achan, the son of Carmi, the son of Zabdi, the son of Zerah, of the tribe of Judah, took of the accursed  thing.        
				        Joshua 7:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (426, 199, 'Achan''s father is Zerah', 'And Joshua, and all Israel with him, took Achan the son of
				          Zerah.... Joshua 7:24
				          
				          Did not Achan the son of Zerah commit a trespass in the
				          accursed thing, and wrath fell on all the congregation of Israel? Joshua 22:20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (427, 200, 'Yes', 'Then Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab, arose and warred against Israel.
				Joshua 24:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (428, 200, 'No', 'And now art thou any thing better than Balak the son of Zippor, 
				king of Moab? did he ever strive against Israel, or did he ever fight against them? 
				Judges 11:25
				
				(This is a rhetorical question whose answer is "No".)', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (429, 201, 'Yes, death is final.', 'This day I [Joshua] am going the way of all the earth. Joshua 23:14

As the cloud is consumed and vanishes away, so he that goeth down to the grave shall come up no more. Job 7:9

Before I go whence I shall not return, even to the land of darkness and the shadow of death; A land of darkness, as darkness itself; and of the shadow of death, without any order, and where the light is as darkness. Job 10:20-21

But man dieth, and wasteth away: yea, man giveth up the ghost, and where is he? ... So man lieth down, and riseth not: till the heavens be no more, they shall not awake, nor be raised out of their sleep ... If a man die, shall he live again? Job 14:10-14

Yet he shall perish for ever like his own dung. Job 20:7

For in death there is no remembrance of thee: in the grave who shall give thee thanks? Psalm 6:5

Let the wicked be ashamed, and let them be silent in the grave. Psalm 31:17

O spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go hence, and be no more. Psalm 39:13

The dead ... whom thou rememberest no more. Psalm 88:5

The dead praise not the LORD, neither any that go down into silence. Psalm 115:17

For that which befalleth the sons of men befalleth beasts; even one thing befalleth them: as the one dieth, so dieth the other; yea, they have all one breath; so that a man hath no preeminence above a beast. Ecclesiastes 3:19

The dead know not anything, neither have they any more a reward. Ecclesiastes 9:5

For there is no work, nor device, nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in the grave, whither thou goest. Ecclesiastes 9:10

They are dead, they shall not live; they are deceased, they shall not rise. Isaiah 26:14

For the grave cannot praise thee, death can not celebrate thee: they that go down into the pit cannot hope for thy truth. Isaiah 38:18

A sinful man ... his glory is dung, and worms ... tomorrow he shall not be found, because he is returned into his earth; and his thought is come to nothing. 1 Machabees 2:62-63', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (430, 201, 'No, there will be a resurrection from the dead.', 'Thy dead men shall live, together with my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust: for thy dew is as the dew of herbs, and the earth shall cast out the dead. Isaiah 26:19

Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, O my people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves, and bring you into the land of Israel. Ezekiel 37:12

And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt. Daniel 12:1

And these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life eternal. Matthew 25:46

Thou shalt be recompensed at the resurrection of the just. Luke 14:14

Marvel not at this: for the hour is coming, in the which all that are in the graves shall hear his voice, And shall come forth; they that have done good, unto the resurrection of life; and they that have done evil, unto the resurrection of damnation. John 5:28-29

That Christ should suffer, and that he should be the first that should rise from the dead. Acts 26:23

For if the dead rise not, then is not Christ raised. 1 Corinthians 15:16

The trumpet shall sound and the dead shall be raised. 1 Corinthians 15:52

This is the promise that he hath promised us, even eternal life. 1 John 2:25

And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before God; ... and they were judged, every man according to their works. Revelation 20:12-13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (431, 202, 'Yes', 'If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, 
				        and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land. 
				        2 Chronicles 7:14
				        
				        I will forgive their iniquity, and I will remember their sin no more. Jeremiah 31:34
				        
				       
				        
If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins. 1 John 1:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (432, 202, 'No', 'God ... will not forgive your transgressions nor your sins. Joshua 24:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (433, 202, 'Only if you forgive others', 'If ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses. 
				Matthew 6:15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (434, 203, 'Jacob', 'And the bones of Joseph, which the children of Israel brought
				          up out of Egypt, buried they in Shechem, in a parcel of ground which Jacob
				          bought of the sons of Hamor. Joshua 24:32', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (435, 203, 'Abraham', 'So Jacob went down into Egypt, and died, he, and our fathers,
				          and were carried over into Shechem, and laid in the sepulchre that Abraham
				          bought for a sum of money of the sons of Hamor. Acts 7:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (436, 204, 'Yes', 'Now the children of Judah had fought against Jerusalem, and had taken it, and smitten 
        it with the edge of the sword, and set the city on fire. Judges 1:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (437, 204, 'No', 'And the children of Benjamin did not drive out the Jebusites that inhabited Jerusalem; but the Jebusites 
        dwell with the children of Benjamin in Jerusalem unto this day. Judges 1:21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (438, 205, 'Sure, he can do anything.', 'And Sisera gathered together all his chariots, even nine hundred chariots of iron, and all the people that were with him, 
				        from Harosheth of the Gentiles unto the river of Kishon. And Deborah said unto Barak, Up; for this is the day in which the LORD 
				        hath delivered Sisera into thine hand: is not the LORD gone out before thee? So Barak went down from mount Tabor, and ten thousand 
				        men after him. And the LORD discomfited Sisera, and all his chariots, 
						and all his host, with the edge of the sword before Barak; 
				        so that Sisera lighted down off his chariot, and fled away on his feet. But Barak pursued after the chariots, and after the host, 
				        unto Harosheth of the Gentiles: and all the host of Sisera fell upon the edge of the sword; and there was not a man left. 
				        Judges 4:13-16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (439, 205, 'No, iron chariots are too hard for him.', 'And the LORD was with Judah; and he drave out the inhabitants of the mountain; but 
						could not drive out the inhabitants of the 
				        valley, because they had chariots of iron. Judges 1:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (440, 206, 'Mary', 'The angel Gabriel was sent from God unto a city of Galilee, named Nazareth, To a virgin espoused to a man whose name was Joseph, of the house of David; and the virgin''s name was Mary. And the angel came in unto her, and said, Hail, thou that art highly favoured, the Lord is with thee: blessed art thou among women. Luke 1:26-28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (441, 206, 'Jael', 'Blessed above women shall Jael ... be, blessed shall she be above women ...  He asked water, and she gave him milk; she brought forth butter in a lordly dish.  She put her hand to the nail, and her right hand to the workmen''s hammer; and with the hammer she smote Sisera, she smote off his head, when she had pierced and stricken through his temples ... there he fell down dead. Judges 5:24-27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (442, 206, 'Judith', 'Blessed art thou ... above all women upon the earth. The Lord ... directed thee to the cutting off the head ... Thy praise shall not depart out of the mouth of men ... for ever.  Judith 13:23-25', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (443, 207, 'Yes, he was fast asleep.', 'Then Jael Heber''s wife took a nail of the tent, and took an hammer in her hand, and went softly unto him, 
			        and smote the nail into his temples, and fastened it  into the ground: for he was fast asleep and weary. So 
			        he died. Judges 4:21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (444, 207, 'No, he was awake and standing up.', 'She put her hand to the nail ... and with the hammer she  smote Sisera.... At her feet he bowed, he fell, 
			        he lay down: at her feet he bowed, he fell: where he bowed, there he fell down dead. Judges 5:26-27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (445, 208, 'Yes, certain kinds of tests are okay.', 'And Gideon said unto
				    God, If thou wilt save Israel by mine hand, as thou hast said, Behold, I will put a
				    fleece of wool in the floor; and if the dew be on the fleece only, and it be
				    dry upon all the earth beside, then shall I know that thou wilt save Israel
				    by mine hand, as thou hast said. And it was so: for
				    he rose up early on the morrow, and thrust the fleece together, and wringed
				    the dew out of the fleece, a bowl full of water. And Gideon said unto
				    God, Let not thine anger be hot against me, and I will speak but this once:
				    let me prove, I pray thee, but this once with the fleece; let it now be dry
				    only upon the fleece, and upon all the ground let there be dew. And God did so that night: for it was dry upon the fleece 
				    only, and there was dew on all the ground. Judges 6:36-40', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (446, 208, 'No, God doesn''t like to be tested or tempted.', 'Ye shall not tempt the Lord your God. Deuteronomy 6:16
				        
				        Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God. Matthew 4:7, 
				        Luke 4:12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (447, 209, '70', 'Gideon had threescore and ten sons of his body begotten: for he had many wives. 
				Judges 8:30', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (448, 209, '72', 'Abimelech ... slew his brethren ... threescore and ten persons, upon one stone. Yet Jotham the youngest son of Jerubbaal 
			[Gideon] was left; for he hid himself. Judges 9:4-5
			
			God sent an evil spirit between Abimelech and the men of Shechem ...  
		 That the cruelty done to the threescore and ten sons of Jerubbaal might come, and their blood be laid upon Abimelech their brother,
		  which slew them; and upon the men of Shechem, which aided him in the killing of his brethren. Judges 9:23-24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (449, 210, 'Yes', 'Boaz took Ruth, and she was his wife: and when he went in unto her, the LORD gave her conception, 
				and she bare a son. ... Tthey called his name Obed: he is the father of Jesse, the father of David. 
				Ruth 4:13-17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (450, 210, 'No', 'The princes came to me, saying, The people of Israel, and the priests, 
				and the Levites, have not separated themselves from the people of the lands, doing according to their abominations, 
				even of ... the Moabites. ...  For they have taken of their daughters for themselves, and for their sons: so that
				 the holy seed have mingled themselves with the people of those lands. ... And when I heard this thing, I rent my garment
				  and my mantle, and plucked off the hair of my head and of my beard, and sat down astonished. Ezra 9:1-3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (451, 211, 'He was a Levite', 'The sons of Levi; Gershon, Kohath, and Merari. 1 Chronicles 6:16

The sons of Kohath; Amminadab his son, Korah his son, Assir his son, 1 Chronicles 6:22

Elkanah his son, and Ebiasaph his son, and Assir his son, 1 Chronicles 6:23

Elkanah knew Hannah his wife; and the LORD remembered her. 1 Samuel 1:19

Hannah had conceived, that she bare a son, and called his name Samuel. 1 Samuel 1:21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (452, 211, 'He was an Ephraimite', 'Now there was a certain man of Ramathaimzophim, of mount Ephraim, and his name was Elkanah, the son of Jeroham, the son of Elihu, the son of Tohu, the son of Zuph, an Ephrathite. 1 Samuel 1:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (453, 212, 'Nothing.', 'He stretcheth out the north over the empty place, and hangeth the earth upon nothing. Job 26:7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (454, 212, 'Pillars.', 'The pillars of the earth are the LORD''s, and he hath set the world upon them. 1 Samuel 2:8
				        
				        Which shaketh the earth out of her place, and the pillars thereof tremble. Job 9:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (455, 213, 'Twenty years.', 'And the men of Kirjathjearim came, and fetched up the ark of the LORD, 
				        and brought it into the  house of Abinadab in the hill, and sanctified Eleazar 
				        his son to keep the ark of the LORD. And it came to pass, while the ark abode 
				        in Kirjathjearim, that the time was long; for it was twenty
				     years: and all the house of Israel lamented after the LORD. 
				     1 Samuel 7:1-2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (456, 213, 'More than forty years.', 'And David arose ... to bring up from thence the ark of God.... And they 
				        set the ark of God upon a new cart, and brought it out of the house of 
				        Abinadab that was in Gibeah.... 2 Samuel 6:2-3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (457, 214, 'Joel.', 'Now the name of his [Samuel''s] firstborn son was Joel. 1 Samuel 8:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (458, 214, 'Vashni.', 'And the sons of Samuel; the firstborn Vashni. 1 Chronicles 6:28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (459, 215, 'No.', 'And ye shall cry out in that day because of your king which ye shall 
				      have chosen you; and the LORD will not hear you in that day. 1 Samuel 8:18
				      
				        Why standest thou afar off, O Lord? why hidest thou thyself
				          in times of trouble?. Psalm 10:1
				
				        
My God, my god, why hast thou forsaken me? why art thou so
				          far from helping me, and from the words of my roaring? O my God, I
				          cry in the daytime, but thou hearest not. Psalm 22:1-2
				          
				          
LORD, why castest thou off my soul? why hidest thou thy face from me? Psalm 88:14
				
				        
And when ye spread forth your hands, I will hide mine eyes
				          from you: yea, when ye make many prayers, I will not hear. Isaiah 1:15
				
				      
Verily thou art a God that hidest thyself. Isaiah 45:15
				 
				      
Thus saith
				    the Lord GOD; Are ye come to enquire of me? As I live, saith the Lord GOD, I
				    will not be enquired of by you. Ezekiel 20:3
				
				        
O LORD, how long shall I cry, and thou wilt not hear! even cry out unto thee of
				     violence, and thou wilt not save! Habakkuk 1:2
				
				      
They shall go with their flocks and with their herds to seek the LORD; but they shall not find him; he hath withdrawn
				     himself from them. Hosea 5:6
				     
				     
Then shall they cry unto the LORD, but he will not hear them: he will even hide his face
				    from them. Micah 3:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (460, 215, 'Yes.', 'For he hath not despised nor abhorred the 
				  affliction of the afflicted; neither hath he hid his face from him; but when he cried unto him, 
				  he heard. Psalm 22:24
				      
				        God is our refuge and our strength, a very present help in
				          trouble. Psalm 46:1
				
				        
The Lord is near to all who call upon him. Psalm 145:18
				
				      
The LORD is good, a strong hold in the day of trouble. Nahum 1:7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (461, 216, 'Abiel', 'Now there was a man of Benjamin, whose name was Kish, the son
				          of Abiel. 1 Samuel 9:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (462, 216, 'Ner', 'And Ner begat Kish. 1 Chronicles 8:33, 9.39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (463, 217, 'Yes', 'So the Philistines were subdued, and they came no more into the coast of Israel: 
				        and the hand of the LORD was against the Philistines all the days of Samuel. 1 Samuel 7:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (464, 217, 'No', 'And the Philistines gathered themselves together to fight with Israel, thirty thousand chariots, 
				        and six thousand horsemen, and people as the sand which is on the sea shore in multitude: and they came up, 
				        and pitched in Michmash, eastward from Bethaven. ... And it came to pass, 
				        that as soon as he had made an end of offering the burnt offering, behold, Samuel came. 1 Samuel 13:5-10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (465, 218, 'The Philistine garrison in Geba', 'And Jonathan smote the garrison of the Philistines that was in Geba. 1 Samuel 13:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (466, 218, 'After the Geba smiting', 'And that first slaughter, which Jonathan and his armourbearer made, was about twenty men, 
				        within as it were an half acre of land. 1 Samuel 14:14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (467, 219, 'Jonathan, Ishui, and Melchishua', 'Now the sons of Saul were Jonathan, and Ishui, and Melchishua. 1 Samuel 14:49', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (468, 219, 'Jonathan, and Malchishua, and Abinadab, and Eshbaal.', 'Saul begat Jonathan, and Malchishua, and Abinadab, and Eshbaal. 
			        1 Chronicles 8:33, 9:39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (469, 220, 'For offering a burnt offering.', 'Saul said, Bring hither a burnt offering to me, and peace offerings. And he offered the burnt offering. 
			        ... 
			        And Samuel said to Saul, Thou hast done foolishly: thou hast not kept the commandment of the LORD thy God ... 
			        But now thy kingdom shall not continue. 1 Samuel 13:9, 13-14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (470, 220, 'For incomplete genocide.', 'Thus saith the LORD of hosts ... go and smite Amalek, and utterly destroy all that they have, and spare them not; 
			        but slay both man and woman, infant and suckling, ox and sheep, camel and ass. 
			        ...
			        And Saul smote the Amalekites ... and utterly destroyed all the people with the edge of the sword. 
			        But Saul and the people spared Agag, and the best of the sheep, and of the oxen, and of the fatlings, and the lambs, 
			        and all that was good, and would not utterly destroy them: but every thing that was vile and refuse, that they destroyed utterly. 
			        
			        Then came the word of the LORD unto Samuel, saying, It repenteth me that I have set up Saul to be king: 
			        for he is turned back from following me, and hath not performed my commandments. 1 Samuel 15:2-3, 7-11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (471, 221, 'Yes', 'After these things did king Ahasuerus promote Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, 
        and advanced him, and set his seat above all the princes that were with him. Esther 3:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (472, 221, 'No', 'Thus saith the LORD of hosts ... Now go and smite Amalek, and utterly destroy all that they have, 
        and spare them not; but slay both man and woman, infant and suckling, ox and sheep, camel and ass. 
        1 Samuel 15:2-3
        
        And Saul smote the Amalekites ... And he took Agag the king of the Amalekites alive, and utterly destroyed all the people 
        with the edge of the sword. 1 Samuel 15:7-8
        
        
Then said Samuel, Bring ye hither to me Agag the king of the Amalekites. And Agag came unto him delicately. And Agag said, 
        Surely the bitterness of death is past. And Samuel said, As the sword hath made women childless, so shall thy mother be childless 
        among women. And Samuel hewed Agag in pieces before the LORD in Gilgal. 1 Samuel 15:32-33', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (473, 222, 'Jesse had eight sons.', 'Jesse made seven of his sons to pass before Samuel. And Samuel
				          said unto Jesse, Are these all thy children? And he said, There
				          remaineth yet the youngest [David]. 1 Samuel 16:10-11
				          
				          Now David was the son of that Ephrathite of Bethlehemjudah, whose name was Jesse; and he had eight sons.
				          1 Samuel 17:12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (474, 222, 'Jesse had seven sons.', 'And Jesse begat his firstborn Eliab, and ... David the seventh. 1 Chronicles 2:13-15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (475, 223, 'Yes', 'Then answered one of the servants, and said, Behold, I have seen a son of Jesse the Bethlehemite, 
				        that is cunning in playing, and a mighty valiant man, and a man of war, and prudent in matters, and a comely person, 
				        and the LORD is with him. 1 Samuel 16:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (476, 223, 'No', 'And Saul said to David, Thou art not able to go against this Philistine to fight with him: for 
				       thou art but a youth, 
				        and he a man of war from his youth. ... And Saul armed David with his armour, and he put an helmet of brass upon 
				        his head; also he armed him with a coat of mail. And David girded his sword upon his armour, 
				        and he assayed to go; 
				        for he had not proved it. And David said unto Saul, I cannot go with these; for I have not proved 
				        them. And David put 
				        them off him. 1 Samuel 17:33-39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (477, 224, 'With a sling only.', 'David put his hand in his bag, and took thence a stone, and slang
				          it, and smote the Philistine in his forehead, that the stone sunk into
				          his forehead; and he fell upon his face to the earth. David prevailed
				          over the Philistine with a sling and with a stone, and smote the
				          Philistine, and slew him; but there was no sword in the hand of
				          David. 1 Samuel 17:49-50', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (478, 224, 'He cut off his head with a sword.', 'David ran, and stood upon the Philistine, and took his sword, and
				          drew it out of the sheath thereof, and slew him,and cut off his
				          head therewith. 1 Samuel 17:51', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (479, 225, 'David killed him twice.', 'David put his hand in his bag, and took thence a stone, and slang it, and smote the Philistine in his forehead, that the stone sunk into his forehead; and he fell upon his face to the earth. David prevailed over the Philistine with a sling and with a stone, and smote the Philistine, and slew him; but there was no sword in the hand of David. 1 Samuel 17:49-50

David ran, and stood upon the Philistine, and took his sword, and drew it out of the sheath thereof, and slew him, and cut off his head therewith. 1 Samuel 17:51

And David said unto Ahimelech ... And the priest said, The sword of Goliath the Philistine, whom thou slewest in the valley of Elah. 1 Samuel 21:8-9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (480, 225, 'Elhanan.', 'And there was again a battle in Gob with the Philistines, where Elhanan the son of Jaareoregim, a Bethlehemite, slew the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the staff of whose spear was like a weaver''s beam. 2 Samuel 21:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (481, 226, 'Before David slew the Philistine.', 'And David came to Saul, and stood before him: and he loved him
			          greatly; and he became his armourbearer. And Saul sent to Jesse,
			          saying, Let David, I pray thee, stand before me; for he hath found
			          favour in my sight. And it came to pass, when the evil spirit from God
			          was upon Saul, that David took an harp, and played with his hand: so
			          Saul was refreshed, and was well, and the evil spirit departed from
			          him. 1 Samuel 16:21-23', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (482, 226, 'After David slew the Philistine.', 'And when Saul saw David go forth against the Philistine, he said
			          unto Abner, the captain of the host, Abner, whose son is this youth?
			          And Abner said, As thy soul liveth, O king, I cannot tell. And the
			          king said, Enquire thou whose son the stripling is. And as David
			          returned from the slaughter of the Philistine, Abner took him, and
			          brought him before Saul with the head of the Philistine in his hand.
			          And Saul said to him, Whose son art thou, thou young man? And David
			          answered, I am the son of thy servant Jesse the Bethlehemite. 1 Samuel 17:55-58', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (483, 227, '100', 'And David sent messengers to Ishbosheth Saul''s son, saying, Deliver me my wife Michal, which I espoused to me for an hundred foreskins of the Philistines. 2 Samuel 3:14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (484, 227, '200', 'Wherefore David arose and went, he and his men, and slew of the Philistines two hundred men; and David brought their foreskins, and they gave them in full tale to the king, that he might be the king''s son in law. And Saul gave him Michal his daughter to wife. 1 Samuel 18:27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (485, 228, 'After the dancing girls sang, "Saul has killed his thousands, and David his tens of thousands."', 'And it came to pass as they came, when David was returned from the slaughter of the Philistine, that the women came 
				        out of all cities of Israel, singing and dancing, to meet king Saul, with tabrets, with joy, and with instruments 
				        of musick. And Saul eyed David from that day and forward. 1 Samuel 18:8-9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (486, 228, 'After David bought Saul''s daughter with 200 Philistine foreskins.', 'Wherefore David arose and went, he and his men, and slew of the Philistines two hundred men; 
				        and David brought their foreskins,  and they gave them in full tale to the king, 
				        that he might be the king''s son in law. And Saul gave him Michal his daughter to wife. 
				        And Saul saw and knew that the LORD was with David, and that Michal Saul''s daughter loved him. 
				        And Saul was yet the more afraid of David; and Saul became David''s enemy continually. 1 Samuel 18:27-29', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (487, 229, 'When Saul prophesied among the prophets.', 'And it came to pass, when all that knew him beforetime saw that, behold, he prophesied among the prophets, 
				        then the people said one to another, What is this that is come unto the son of Kish? Is Saul also among the prophets? 
				        And one of the same place answered and said, But who is their father? Therefore it became a proverb, 
				        Is Saul also among the prophets? 1 Samuel 10:11-12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (488, 229, 'After Saul prophesied naked for a day and a night.', 'And he stripped off his clothes also, and prophesied before Samuel in like manner, and lay down naked all that day and all that night. 
				        Wherefore they say, Is Saul also among the prophets? 1 Samuel 19:24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (489, 230, 'After he hacked Agag to pieces', 'And Samuel came no more to see Saul until the day of his death: nevertheless Samuel mourned for Saul: 
				        and the LORD repented that he had made Saul king over Israel. 1 Samuel 15:35', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (490, 230, 'When Saul prophesied naked', 'And he stripped off his clothes also, and prophesied before Samuel in like manner, and lay down naked all that day and 
				        all that night. Wherefore they say, Is Saul also among the prophets? 1 Samuel 19:24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (491, 231, 'Ahimelech', 'Then David came to Nob to Ahimelech the priest. 1 Samuel 21:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (492, 231, 'Abiathar', 'Have ye never read what David did ... How he went into the
			          house of God in the days of Abiathar the high priest? Mark 2:25-26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (493, 232, 'He was alone.', 'Then came David to Nob to Ahimelech the priest: and Ahimelech was afraid at the meeting of David, and said unto him, Why art thou alone, and no man with thee? 1 Samuel 21:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (494, 232, 'He was with others.', 'But he said unto them, Have ye not read what David did, when he was an hungred, and they that were with him; How he entered into the house of God, and did eat the shewbread, which was not lawful for him to eat, neither for them which were with him, but only for the priests? Matthew 12:3-4

And he said unto them, Have ye never read what David did, when he had need, and was an hungred, he, and they that were with him? How he went into the house of God in the days of Abiathar the high priest, and did eat the shewbread, which is not lawful to eat but for the priests, and gave also to them which were with him? Mark 2:25-26

And Jesus answering them said, Have ye not read so much as this, what David did, when himself was an hungred, and they which were with him; How he went into the house of God, and did take and eat the shewbread, and gave also to them that were with him; which it is not lawful to eat but for the priests alone? Luke 6:3-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (495, 233, 'Abiathar was the son of Ahimelech.', 'And one of the sons of Ahimelech the son of Ahitub, named Abiathar. 1 Samuel 22:20

Abiathar the son of Ahimelech. 1 Samuel 23:6

And David said to Abiathar the priest, Ahimelech''s son. 1 Samuel 30:7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (496, 233, 'Abiathar was the father of Ahimelech.', 'Ahimelech the son of Abiathar. 2 Samuel 8:17, 1 Chronicles 18:16, 24:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (497, 234, 'Saul inquired of the Lord.', 'And when Saul inquired of the Lord, the Lord answered
				          him not. 1 Samuel 28:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (498, 234, 'Saul did not inquire of the Lord.', 'So Saul ... inquired not of the Lord: wherefore he slew him. 1 Chronicles 10:13-14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (499, 235, 'Jesus was the first person to rise from the dead.', 'That Christ should suffer, and that he should be the first that should rise from the dead. Acts 26:23

But now is Christ risen from the dead, and become the firstfruits of them that slept. 1 Corinthians 15:20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (500, 235, 'Others rose from the dead before him.', 'Then said the woman, Whom shall I bring up unto thee? And he said, Bring me up Samuel .... And he said unto her, What form is he of? And she said, An old man cometh up; and he is covered with a mantle. And Saul perceived that it was Samuel. 1 Samuel 28:11, 14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (501, 236, 'Yes', 'And Saul smote the Amalekites from Havilah until thou comest to Shur, that is over against Egypt. And he took Agag 
				        the king of the Amalekites alive, and utterly destroyed all the people with the edge of the sword. ...
				         And Samuel hewed Agag in pieces before the LORD in Gilgal. 
				        1 Samuel 15:7-8, 33', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (502, 236, 'No, Agag''s mother was left alive.', 'And Samuel said, As the sword hath made women childless, so shall thy mother be childless among women. 
				1 Samuel 15:33', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (503, 236, 'No, David killed them all a few years later.', 'And David and his men went up, and invaded the Geshurites, and the Gezrites, and the Amalekites: 
				    for those nations were of old the inhabitants of the land, as thou goest to Shur, even unto the land of Egypt. 
				    And David smote the land, and left neither man nor woman alive, and took away the sheep, and the oxen, and the asses, 
				    and the camels, and the apparel, and returned, and came to Achish. 1 Samuel 27:8-9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (504, 236, 'And then David killed them all again, just to make sure. (Except this time 400 guys escaped.)', 'And it came to pass, when David and his men were come to Ziklag on the third day, that the Amalekites had invaded 
				the south, and Ziklag, and smitten Ziklag, and burned it with fire; . . . And David smote them from the twilight even unto 
				the evening of the next day: and there escaped not a man of them, save four hundred young men, which rode upon camels, 
				and fled. 1 Samuel 30:1, 17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (505, 236, 'No, Saul was killed by an Amalekite.', 'I am an Amalekite. ... So I stood upon him, and slew him. 2 Samuel 1:8-10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (506, 237, 'Saul committed suicide.', 'Therefore Saul took a sword, and fell upon it. So Saul
			          died. 1 Samuel 31:4-6
			                    
			         Then said Saul to his armourbearer, Draw thy sword, and thrust me through therewith; lest these
			     uncircumcised come and abuse me. But his armourbearer would not; for he was sore afraid. So
			     Saul took a sword, and fell upon it. 1 Chronicles 10:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (507, 237, 'Saul was killed by an Amalekite.', 'And he [Saul] said unto me, Who art thou? And I answered him,
			          I am an Amalekite. He said unto me again, Stand, I pray thee, upon me,
			          and slay me. So I stood upon him, and slew him. 2 Samuel 1:8-10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (508, 237, 'Saul was killed by the Philistines.', 'The Philistines had slain Saul. 2 Samuel 21:12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (509, 237, 'God killed him.', 'So Saul died for his transgression which he committed against the LORD, 
			      even against the word of the LORD, which he kept not, and also for asking 
			      counsel of one that had a familiar spirit, to enquire of it; 
			     And enquired not of the LORD: therefore he slew him, and turned the kingdom unto
			     David the son of Jesse. 1 Chronicles 10:14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (510, 238, 'Yes, all of Saul''s family died with him.', 'So Saul died, and his three sons, and all his house died together. 1 Chronicles 10:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (511, 238, 'No, one of Saul''s sons (Ishbosheth) became king of Israel after Saul died.', 'Your master Saul is dead .... But Abner ... took Ishbosheth  the son of Saul, and brought him over to Mahanaim and made him
			          king. 2 Samuel 2:1-7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (512, 238, 'No, David sacrificed two of Saul''s sons and five of his grandsons to God to stop him from starving people to death.', 'Then there was a famine in the days of David three years, year after year; and David enquired of the LORD. And the LORD 
			      answered, It is for Saul, and for his bloody house, because he slew the Gibeonites. ...Wherefore David said unto the Gibeonites, 
			      What shall I do for you? and wherewith shall I make the atonement? ... And they answered the king ... Let seven men of his sons be 
			      delivered unto us, and we will hang them up unto the LORD ... And the king said, I will give them. ... 
				The king took the two sons 
			      of Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, whom she bare unto Saul, Armoni and Mephibosheth; and the five sons of Michal the daughter of Saul ... 
			      And he delivered them into the hands of the Gibeonites, and they hanged them in the hill before the LORD: and they fell all 
			      seven together, and were put to death. ... And after that God was intreated for the land. 2 Samuel 21:1-14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (513, 239, 'Chileab', 'And unto David were sons born in Hebron: and his firstborn was Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess; And his second, Chileab, of Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite. 2 Samuel 3:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (514, 239, 'Daniel', 'Now these were the sons of David, which were born unto him in Hebron; the firstborn Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess; the second Daniel, of Abigail the Carmelitess. 1 Chronicles 3:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (515, 240, 'Amnon, Chileab, Absalom, Adonijah, Shephatiah, Ithream.', 'And unto David were sons born in Hebron: and his firstborn was Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess;
				
				And his second, Chileab, of Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite; and the third, Absalom the son of Maacah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur;
				
				And the fourth, Adonijah the son of Haggith; and the fifth, Shephatiah the son of Abital;
				
				And the sixth, Ithream, by Eglah David''s wife. These were born to David in Hebron. 2 Samuel 3:2-5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (516, 240, 'Amnon, Daniel, Absalom, Adonijah, Shephatiah, Ithream.', 'Now these were the sons of David, which were born unto him in Hebron; the firstborn Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess; 
				   the second Daniel, of Abigail the Carmelitess:
				
				The third, Absalom the son of Maachah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur: the fourth, Adonijah the son of Haggith:
				
				The fifth, Shephatiah of Abital: the sixth, Ithream by Eglah his wife.
				
				These six were born unto him in Hebron. 1 Chronicles 3:1-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (517, 242, 'God killed Uzzah at the threshingfloor of Nachon.', 'And when they came to Nachon''s threshingfloor, Uzzah
				          put forth his hand to the ark of God, and took hold of it; for the
				          oxen shook it. And the anger of the Lord was kindled against Uzzah,
				          and God smote him. 2 Samuel 6:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (518, 242, 'God killed Uzzah at the threshingfloor of Chidon.', 'And when they came unto the threshingfloor of Chidon,
				          Uzza put forth his hand to hold the ark, for the oxen stumbled. And
				          the anger of the Lord was kindled against Uzza, and he smote
				          him. 1 Chronicles 13:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (519, 243, '700', 'And David took from him a thousand chariots and seven
			          hundred horsemen. 2 Samuel 8:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (520, 243, '7000', 'And David took from him a thousand chariots and seven
			          thousand horsemen. 1 Chronicles 18:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (521, 244, '700 men in chariots and 40,000 horsemen', 'And David slew the men of seven hundred chariots of the
				          Syrians, and forty thousand horsemen. 2 Samuel 10:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (522, 244, '7000 men in chariots and 40,000 footmen', 'David slew of the Syrians seven thousand men which
				          fought in chariots, and forty thousand footmen. 1 Chronicles 19:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (523, 245, 'After forty years', 'And it came to pass after forty years, that Absalom said unto the king, I
				    pray thee, let me go and pay my vow, which I have vowed unto the LORD, in
				    Hebron. ... But Absalom sent spies throughout all the tribes of Israel, saying, 
				    As soon as ye hear the sound of the trumpet, then ye shall say, 
				    Absalom reigneth in Hebron. 2 Samuel 15:7-10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (524, 245, 'Less than forty years since David only ruled for a total of forty years.', 'David was thirty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned forty
				    years. 2 Samuel 5:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (525, 246, 'Amasa''s father was Ithra an Israelite.', 'Amasa was a man''s son, whose name was Ithra an Israelite. 2 Samuel 17:25', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (526, 246, 'Amasa''s father was Jether an Ishmaelite.', 'And the father of Amasa was Jether the Ishmaelite. 1 Chronicles 2:17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (527, 247, 'Absalom had no sons.', 'Now Absalom ... said, I have not son to keep my name in
				          remembrance. 2 Samuel 18:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (528, 247, 'Absalom had three sons.', 'And unto Absalom there were born three sons. 2 Samuel 14:27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (529, 248, 'Michal had no child.', 'And Michal the daughter of Saul came out to meet David, and said, How glorious was the king of Israel to day, who uncovered himself to day in the eyes of the handmaids of his servants, as one of the vain fellows shamelessly uncovereth himself! ... Therefore Michal the daughter of Saul had no child unto the day of her death. 2 Samuel 6:20-23', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (530, 248, 'Michal had five children.', 'There was a famine in the days of David three years, year after year; and David enquired of the LORD. And the LORD answered, It is for Saul, and for his bloody house, because he slew the Gibeonites. ... Let seven men of his sons be delivered unto us, and we will hang them up unto the LORD. ... And the king said, I will give them. ... The king took the two sons of Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, whom she bare unto Saul, Armoni and Mephibosheth; and the five sons of Michal the daughter of Saul. ... And he delivered them into the hands of the Gibeonites, and they hanged them in the hill before the LORD. ... And after that God was intreated for the land. 2 Samuel 21:1-14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (531, 249, 'Goliath', 'And there was again a battle in Gob with the Philistines, where Elhanan the 
				  son of Jaareoregim, a Bethlehemite, slew the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the staff of whose spear was like a
				    weaver''s beam. 2 Samuel 21:19
				    
				    [The words "the brother of" were inserted by the KJV translators to avoid the obvious contradiction with 
				    1 Samuel 17:49-51.]', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (532, 249, 'Lahmi, the brother of Goliath', 'And there was war again with the Philistines; and Elhanan the son of Jair slew Lahmi the brother of Goliath the Gittite, whose 
				        spear staff was like a weaver''s beam. 1 Chronicles 20:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (533, 250, 'David never sinned.', 'The LORD rewarded me [David] according to my righteousness: according to the
				    cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me. 2 Samuel:22:21
				    
				  Therefore the LORD hath recompensed me according to my righteousness; according to my cleanness in his eye sight. 
				  2 Samuel 22:25', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (534, 250, 'David never sinned, except in the matter of Uriah.', 'David did that which was right in the eyes of the Lord,
				          and turned not aside from anything that he commanded him all the
				          days of his life, save only in the matter of Uriah the Hittite. 1 Kings 15:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (535, 250, 'David sinned in numbering the people.', 'And David''s heart smote him after that he had numbered the
				          people. And David said unto the Lord, I have sinned greatly in
				          that I have done. 2 Samuel 24:10, 
				          1 Chronicles 21:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (536, 252, '36', 'These be the names of the mighty men whom David had ... thirty and seven in all. 
				2 Samuel 23:8-39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (537, 252, '37', 'These be the names of the mighty men whom David had ... thirty and seven in all. 
				2 Samuel 23:8-39', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (538, 253, '800,000 for Israel; 500,000 for Judah.', 'And Joab gave up the sum of the number of the people unto the king; and there were in Israel eight hundred thousand valiant men that drew the sword; and the men of Judah five hundred thousand men. 2 Samuel 24:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (539, 253, '1,100,000 for Israel; 470,000 for Judah.', 'And Joab gave the sum of the number of the people unto David. And all they of Israel were a thousand thousand and a hundred thousand [1,100,000] men that drew sword; and Judah was four hundred three score and ten thousand [470,000] men that drew the sword. 1 Chronicles 21:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (540, 254, 'Seven years of famine', 'So Gad came to David and told him, Shall seven years of
			          famine come unto thee in thy land? 2 Samuel 24:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (541, 254, 'Three years of famine', 'So Gad came to David and said unto him, Thus saith the Lord,
			          choose thee either three years of famine. 1 Chronicles 21:11-12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (542, 255, 'For fifty shekels of silver.', 'So David bought the threshing floor and the oxen for fifty shekel of silver. 2 Samuel 24:24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (543, 255, 'For six hundred shekels of gold.', 'So David gave to Ornan for the place six hundred shekels of gold. 1 Chronicles 21:25', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (544, 256, 'Yes', 'And the king went to Gibeon to sacrifice there; for that was the great high place: a thousand burnt offerings did Solomon offer upon that altar. 
				 1 Kings 3:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (545, 256, 'No, everyone in Israel was with him.', 'Solomon, and all the congregation with him, went to the high place that was at Gibeon. ... 
				
				And Solomon ... offered a thousand burnt offerings upon it. 2 Chronicles 1:3-6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (546, 257, 'Solomon', 'I have given thee [Solomon] a wise and an
					     understanding heart; so that there was none like thee before thee, neither after thee
					     shall any arise like unto thee. 1 Kings 3:12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (547, 257, 'Jesus', 'I indeed baptize you with water unto repentance. but he that cometh after me is mightier than I, 
					    whose shoes I am not worthy to bear. Matthew 3:11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (548, 257, 'John the Baptist', 'Among them that are born of women there hath not risen a greater than 
					  John the Baptist. Matthew 11:11
					  
					  Among those that are born of women there is not a greater prophet than John the Baptist. 
					  Luke 7:28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (549, 257, 'Everyone in the kingdom of heaven.', 'Among them that are born of women there hath not risen a greater than 
					  John the Baptist: Among them that are born of women there hath not risen a greater than John the Baptist: 
					  notwithstanding he that is least in the kingdom of heaven is greater than he. Matthew 11:11
					  
					  Among those that are born of women there is not a greater prophet than John the Baptist: but 
					  he that is least in the kingdom of God is greater than he.  Luke 7:28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (550, 257, 'Whoever is as humble as a little child', 'At the same time came the disciples unto Jesus, saying, Who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?
					  And Jesus called a little child unto him, and set him in the midst of them, 
					  And said, Verily I say unto you, Except ye be converted, and become as little children, ye shall 
					  not enter into the kingdom of heaven.
					  Whosoever therefore shall humble himself as this little child, the same is greatest in the kingdom of heaven.
					  Matthew 18:1-4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (551, 258, 'Solomon had 40,000 stalls.', 'And Solomon had forty thousand stalls of horses for his
			          chariots. 1 Kings 4:26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (552, 258, 'Solomon had 4,000 stalls.', 'And Solomon had four thousand stalls for horses and
			          chariots. 2 Chronicles 9:25', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (553, 259, 'Mahol', 'For he [Solomon] was wiser than all men; than Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and Chalcol, and Darda, the sons of Mahol...  
			    1 Kings 4:31', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (554, 259, 'Zerah', 'And the sons of Zerah; Zimri, and Ethan, and Heman, and Calcol, and Dara: five of them in all. 
			        1 Chronicles 2:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (555, 259, 'Joel', 'Heman a singer, the son of Joel...  1 Chronicles 6:33
			        
			        Heman the son of Joel...  1 Chronicles 15:17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (556, 260, 'Wheat and oil', 'And Solomon gave Hiram twenty thousand measures of wheat for food to his household, 
				        and twenty measures of pure oil: thus gave Solomon to Hiram year by year. 1 Kings 5:11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (557, 260, 'Wheat, barley, wine, and oil.', 'And, behold, I will give to thy servants, the hewers that cut timber, twenty thousand measures of beaten wheat, 
				        and twenty thousand measures of barley, and twenty thousand baths of wine, and twenty thousand baths of oil. 
				        2 Chronicles 2:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (558, 261, 'Solomon had 3,300 overseers.', 'Besides the chief of Solomon''s officers which were over the
				          work, three thousand and three hundred, which ruled over the
				          people that wrought the work. 1 Kings 5:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (559, 261, 'Solomon had 3,600 overseers.', 'And he [Solomon] set ... three thousand and six hundred
				          overseers to set the people to work. 2 Chronicles 2:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (560, 262, '476 years after the Israelites left Egypt', 'And it came to pass in the four hundred and eightieth year after the children of Israel were come out of the land of Egypt, in the fourth year of Solomon''s reign over Israel, in the month Zif, which is the second month, that he began to build the house of the LORD. 1 Kings 6:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (561, 262, '570 years after the Israelites left Egypt', 'The God of this people of Israel chose our fathers, and exalted the people when they dwelt as strangers in the land of Egypt, and with an high arm brought he them out of it. And about the time of forty years suffered he their manners in the wilderness. And when he had destroyed seven nations in the land of Chanaan, he divided their land to them by lot. And after that he gave unto them judges about the space of four hundred and fifty years, until Samuel the prophet. And afterward they desired a king: and God gave unto them Saul the son of Cis, a man of the tribe of Benjamin, by the space of forty years. And when he had removed him, he raised up unto them David to be their king. Acts 13:17-22

Thus David the son of Jesse reigned over all Israel. And the time that he reigned over Israel was forty years; seven years reigned he in Hebron, and thirty and three years reigned he in Jerusalem. 1 Chronicles 29:26-27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (562, 263, 'The tribe of Naphtali', 'And king Solomon sent and fetched Hiram out of Tyre. He was a widow''s son of the tribe of Naphtali, 
				  and his father was a man of Tyre, a worker in brass: and he was filled with wisdom, and understanding, 
				  and cunning to work all works in brass. And he came to king Solomon, and wrought all his work. 
				  1 Kings 7:13-14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (563, 263, 'The tribe of Dan', 'Huram  ... the son of a woman of the daughters of Dan, and his father was a man of Tyre, skilful to work in gold, 
				        and in silver, in brass, in iron, in stone, and in timber, in purple, in blue, and in fine linen, and in crimson. 
				        2 Chronicles 2:13-14', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (564, 264, 'The pillars of brass were 18 cubits high.', 'For he cast two pillars of brass, of eighteen cubits
			          high. 1 Kings 7:15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (565, 264, 'The pillars were 35 cubits high.', 'Also he made before the house two pillars of thirty and
			          five cubits high. 2 Chronicles 3:15', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (566, 265, '2000 baths', 'It contained two thousand baths. 1 Kings 7.26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (567, 265, '3000 baths', 'It received and held three thousand baths. 2 Chronicles 4:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (568, 266, 'God dwells in darkness.', 'The Lord said that he would dwell in the thick darkness. 1 Kings 8:12, 2 Chronicles 6:1
			      
			        He made darkness his secret place; his pavilion round
			          about him were dark waters and thick clouds of the skies. Psalm 18:11
			     
			       
Clouds and darkness are round about him. Psalm 97:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (569, 266, 'God dwells in light.', 'Lord of lords; who only hath immortality, dwelling in the
			          light. 1 Timothy 6:15-16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (570, 267, 'God dwells in temples.', 'I have surely built thee [God] an house to dwell in. 1 Kings 8:13
			        
			        I [God] ... have chosen this place to myself for a house. That
			          my name may be there for ever: and mine eyes and mine heart shall be
			          there perpetually.2 Chronicles 7:12, 16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (571, 267, 'God does not dwell in temples.', 'The Most High dwelleth not in temples made with hands. Acts 7:48
			        
			        
He is Lord of heaven and earth, dwelleth not in temples. Acts 17:24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (572, 268, 'Yes, everyone is a sinner.', 'There is no man that sinneth not. 1 Kings 8:46
				        
				        There is no man which sinneth not. 2 Chronicles 6:36
				        
				        
Who can say, I have made my heart clean, I am pure from my sin. Proverbs 20:9
				        
				        
For there is not a just man upon earth, that doeth good, and
				          sinneth not. Ecclesiastes 7:20
				          
				          
For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God. Romans 3:23
				        
				        
If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the
				          truth is not in us. 1 John 1:8
				          
				        
If we say that we have not sinned, we
				      make him a liar, and his word is not in us. 1 John 1:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (573, 268, 'No, Christians are sinless.', 'Death  reigned from Adam to Moses, even over them that had not sinned. Romans 5:14
				      
				        Whosoever abideth in him sinneth not. 1 John 3:6
				        
				        
Whosoever is born of God doth not commit sin; for his seed remaineth in 
				        him: and he cannot sin, because he is born of God. 1 John 3:9
				        
				        
We know that whosoever is born of God sinneth not. 1 John 5:18
				         
				       
He that doeth good is of God: but he that doeth evil hath not seen God. 3 John 11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (574, 269, '550', 'These were the chief of the officers that were over Solomon''s
			          work, five hundred and fifty. 1 Kings 9:23', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (575, 269, '250', 'And these were the chief of king Solomon''s officers, even two
			          hundred and fifty. 2 Chronicles 8:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (576, 270, '420', 'And Hiram sent in the navy his servants ... and they came to
			          Ophir, and fetched from thence gold, four hundred and twenty
			          talents, and brought it to Solomon. 1 Kings 9:27-28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (577, 270, '450', 'And Huram sent him ... four hundred and fifty talents
			          of gold, and brought them to king Solomon. 2 Chronicles 8:18', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (578, 271, 'Yes.', 'Behold, I will bring evil upon the house of Jeroboam, and will cut off from Jeroboam him that pisseth against the wall. 
			  	1 Kings 14:10
			  
			      
Behold, this evil is of the Lord. 2 Kings 6:33
			      
			      
I will bring evil from the north. Jeremiah 4:6
			      
			      
Behold, I frame evil against you. Jeremiah 18:11
			      
			      
I ... create evil. Isaiah 45:7
			        
			        
What? shall we receive good at the hand of God, and shall we not receive evil? Job 2:10
			        
			        
Out of the mouth of the most High proceedeth not evil and good? Lamentations 3:38
			
			       
Shall there be evil in a city, and the LORD hath not done it? Amos 3:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (579, 271, 'No.', 'For thou art not a God that hath pleasure in wickedness: neither shall evil dwell with thee. Psalm 5:4
			        
			        God is love. 1 John 4:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (580, 272, 'He died peacefully.', 'And the days which Jeroboam reigned were two and twenty years: and he slept with his fathers. 1 Kings 14;20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (581, 272, 'God killed him.', 'Neither did Jeroboam recover strength again in the days of Abijah: and the LORD struck him, and he died. 2 Chronicles 13:20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (582, 273, 'Maachah, the daughter of Abishalom', 'Now in the eighteenth year of king Jeroboam the son of Nebat reigned Abijam over Judah. 
			        Three years reigned he in Jerusalem. And his mother''s name was Maachah, the daughter of 
			        Abishalom. 1 Kings 15:1-2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (583, 273, 'Michaiah the daughter of Uriel', 'Now in the eighteenth year of king Jeroboam began Abijah to reign over
			    Judah. Three years reigned he in Jerusalem. His mother''s 
			    name also was Michaiah the daughter of Uriel. 2 Chronicles 13:1-2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (584, 274, 'Abijam was Asa''s father.', 'And Abijam slept with his fathers; and they buried him in the city of
				    David: and Asa his son reigned in his stead. 1 Kings 15:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (585, 274, 'Abijam was Asa''s brother.', 'Now in the eighteenth year of king Jeroboam the son of Nebat reigned Abijam over Judah. 
				        Three years reigned he in Jerusalem. And his mother''s name was Maachah, the 
				  daughter of Abishalom. 1 Kings 15:1-2
				    
				        And in the twentieth year of Jeroboam king of Israel reigned Asa over
				    Judah. And forty and one years reigned he in Jerusalem. And his mother''s name was
				    Maachah, the daughter of Abishalom. 1 Kings 15:9-10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (586, 275, 'Asa removed the high places.', 'Also he [Asa] took away out of all the cities of Judah the
				          high places. 2 Chronicles 14:3-5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (587, 275, 'Asa did not remove the high places.', 'But the high places were not removed: nevertheless
				          Asa''s heart was perfect with the Lord all his days. 1 Kings 15:14
				          
				        But the high places were not taken away out of Israel:
				          nevertheless the heart of Asa was perfect all his days. 2 Chronicles 15:17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (588, 276, 'In the 26th year of King Asa''s reign.', 'So Baasha slept with his fathers, and was buried in Tirzah: and Elah his son reigned in his stead.... 
				        In the twenty and sixth year of Asa king of Judah began Elah the son of Baasha to reign over Israel in Tirzah, two years. 
				        1 Kings 16:6-8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (589, 276, 'Sometime after the 36th year of King Asa''s reign.', 'In the six and thirtieth year of the reign of Asa Baasha king of Israel came up against Judah, and built Ramah. 
				        2 Chronicles 16:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (590, 277, 'Jehu was the son of Nimshi.', 'And Jehu the son of Nimshi shalt thou anoint to be
				          king. 1 Kings 19:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (591, 277, 'Jehu was the grandson of Nimshi.', 'And when thou commest thither, look out there Jehu the son
				          of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi and go in. 2 Kings 9:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (592, 278, 'Before', 'So he ... found Elisha ... and Elijah passed by him, and cast his mantle upon him. 1 Kings 19:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (593, 278, 'After', 'Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven. He [Elisha] took up also the mantle of Elijah that fell from him. 2 Kings 2:11-13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (594, 279, 'No', 'He [Ahab] rent his clothes, and put sackcloth upon his flesh, and fasted, and lay in sackcloth, and went softly. And the word of the LORD came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying, Seest thou how Ahab humbleth himself before me? because he humbleth himself before me, I will not bring the evil in his days: but in his son''s days will I bring the evil upon his house. 1 Kings 21:27-29', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (595, 279, 'Yes', 'Thus saith the LORD, Because thou hast let go out of thy hand a man whom I appointed to utter destruction, therefore thy life shall go for his life, and thy people for his people. 1 Kings 20:42', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (596, 280, 'Yes.', 'Jehoshaphat ... took away the high places. 2 Chronicles 17:5-6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (597, 280, 'No.', 'Jehoshaphat ... walked in all the ways of Asa his father; he
			          turned not aside from it, doing that which was right in the eyes of
			          the LORD: nevertheless the high places were not taken away. 1 Kings 22:42-43
			
			        Jehoshaphat ... walked in the say of Asa his father, and
			          departed not from it, doing that which was right in the eyes of the
			          Lord. Howbeit the high places were not taken away. 2 Chronicles 20:31-33', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (598, 281, 'No one has ascended into heaven.', 'No man hath ascended up to heaven, but he that came down from heaven, even the 
				        Son of man which is in heaven. John 3:13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (599, 281, 'Some have ascended into heaven.', 'And Enoch walked with God: and he was not; For God took
				          him. Genesis 5:24 
				          
				          Enoch was translated that he should not see death; and was not
				          found, because God had translated him. Hebrews 11:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (600, 282, 'Yes', 'Honour thy father and thy mother. Exodus 20:12, 
				        Deuteronomy 5:16, Ephesians 6:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (601, 282, 'No, you have no father but God.', 'Call no man your father upon the earth: for one is your
				          Father, which is in heaven. Matthew 23:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (602, 283, 'Yes', 'Because ... thou ... hast rent thy clothes ... I also have heard thee, saith the LORD. 
				2 Kings 22:19
				
				Because thine heart was tender ... and didst rend thy clothes, and weep before me; I have even heard thee also, 
				saith the LORD. 2 Chronicles 34:27
				
				
				A time to rend. Ecclesiastes 3:7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (603, 283, 'No', 'Rend your hearts, not your garments. Joel 2:12-13
				
				When Elisha the man of God had heard that the king of Israel had rent his clothes, 
        that he sent to the king, saying, Wherefore hast thou rent thy clothes? 2 Kings 5:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (604, 284, 'Yes', 'The leprosy therefore of Naaman shall cleave unto thee, and unto thy seed for ever. 
			        And he went out from his presence a leper as white as snow. 2 Kings 5:27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (605, 284, 'No', 'And the king talked with Gehazi the servant of the man of God, saying, Tell me, I pray thee, 
			        all the great things that Elisha hath done. 2 Kings 8:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (606, 285, 'Omri', 'Two and twenty years old was Ahaziah when he began to reign; and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. And his mother''s name was Athaliah, the daughter of Omri king of Israel. 2 Kings 8:26

Forty and two years old was Ahaziah when he began to reign, and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother''s name also was Athaliah the daughter of Omri. 2 Chronicles 22:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (607, 285, 'Ahab', 'And he [Jehoram, Athaliah''s husband] walked in the way of the kings of Israel, as did the house of Ahab: for the daughter of Ahab was his wife: and he did evil in the sight of the LORD. 2 Kings 8:18

And he walked in the way of the kings of Israel, like as did the house of Ahab: for he had the daughter of Ahab to wife: and he wrought that which was evil in the eyes of the LORD. 2 Chronicles 21:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (608, 286, '22 years old', 'Two and twenty years old was Ahaziah when he began to
          reign. 2 Kings 8:26', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (609, 286, '42 years old', 'Forty and two years old was Ahaziah when he began to
          reign. 2 Chronicles 22:2', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (610, 287, 'In the twelfth year of Joram.', 'In the twelfth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of
			          Israel did Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah begin to
			          reign. 2 Kings 8:25', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (611, 287, 'In the eleventh year of Joram.', 'And in the eleventh year of Joram the son of Ahab began
			          Ahaziah to reign. 2 Kings 9:29', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (612, 288, 'God commended him for it.', 'Thus saith the Lord God of Israel, I have anointed thee king over the people of the Lord, even over Israel. And thou shalt smite the house of Ahab thy master, that I may avenge the blood of my servants the prophets, and the blood of all the servants of the Lord, at the hand of Jezebel. For the whole house of Ahab shall perish: and I will cut off from Ahab him that pisseth against the wall. 2 Kings 9:6-8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (613, 288, 'God condemned him for it.', 'And the LORD said unto him, Call his name Jezreel; for yet a little while, and I will avenge the blood of Jezreel upon the house of Jehu, and will cause to cease the kingdom of the house of Israel. Hosea 1:4', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (614, 289, 'With the other kings in Jerusalem.', 'Joash ... died; and they buried him with his fathers in
				          the city of David. 2 Kings 12:20-21', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (615, 289, 'In Jerusalem, but not with the other kings.', 'Joash ... died: and they buried him in the city of David, but
				          they buried him not in the sepulchres of the kings. 2 Chronicles 24:24-25', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (616, 290, 'At least forty years after Joash became king of Judah.', 'In the three and twentieth year of Joash the son of Ahaziah
				          king of Judah Jehoahaz the son of Jehu began to reign over Israel in
				          Samaria, and reigned seventeen years. 2 Kings 13:1', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (617, 290, 'In the thirty seventh year of Joash''s reign.', 'In the thirty and seventh year of Joash king of Judah began
				          Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz to reign over Israel in Samaria. 2 Kings 13:10', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (618, 291, 'Joram was Uzziah''s father.', 'Joram begat Ozias [Uzziah]. Matthew 1:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (619, 291, 'Joram was Uzziah''s [Azariah''s] great-great-grandfather.', 'And Solomon''s son was Rehoboam, Abia his son, Asa his son, Jehoshaphat his son, Joram his son, Ahaziah his son, Joash his son, Amaziah his son, Azariah his son. 1 Chronicles 3:10-12', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (620, 292, 'Yes', 'Samaria shall become desolate; for she hath rebelled against her God: they shall fall by the sword: their infants shall be dashed in pieces, and their women with child shall be ripped up. Hosea 13:16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (621, 292, 'No', 'Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of the children of Ammon, and for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they have ripped up the women with child of Gilead, that they might enlarge their border. Amos 1:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (622, 293, 'At least 20 years.', '... in the twentieth year of Jotham the son of Uzziah. 2 Kings 15:30', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (623, 293, '16 years.', 'Jotham the son of Uzziah  ... reigned sixteen  years in Jerusalem. 2 Kings15:32-33', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (624, 294, 'Yes.', 'And Ahaz slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the
				    city of David. 2 Kings 16:20', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (625, 294, 'No.', 'And Ahaz slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the city, even in
				    Jerusalem: but they brought him not into the sepulchres of the kings of
				    Israel. 2 Chronicles 28:27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (626, 295, 'Hezekiah', 'He trusted in the LORD God of Israel; so that after him was none like him among all the kings of Judah, nor any that were before him. 2 Kings 18:5', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (627, 295, 'Josiah', 'And like unto him [Josiah] was there no king before him, that turned to the LORD with all his heart, and with all his soul, and with all his might, according to all the law of Moses; neither after him arose there any like him. 2 Kings 23:25', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (628, 296, 'As a sign that he would heal Hezekiah''s boil', 'And Isaiah said, Take a lump of figs. And they took and laid it on the boil, and he recovered. And Hezekiah said unto Isaiah, 
				        What shall be the sign that the LORD will heal me, and that I shall go up into the house of the LORD the third day? And Isaiah said, 
				        This sign shalt thou have of the LORD, that the LORD will do the thing that he hath spoken: shall the shadow go forward ten degrees, 
				        or go back ten degrees? And Hezekiah answered, It is a light thing for the shadow to go down ten degrees: nay, but let the shadow 
				        return backward ten degrees. And Isaiah the prophet cried unto the LORD: and he brought the shadow ten degrees backward, 
				        by which it had gone down in the dial of Ahaz. 2 Kings 20:7-11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (629, 296, 'As a sign that he would defend the city against the Assyrians', 'Then came the word of the LORD to Isaiah, saying, Go, and say to Hezekiah, Thus saith the LORD, the God of David thy father, 
				        I have heard thy prayer, I have seen thy tears: behold, I will add unto thy days fifteen years. And I will deliver thee and this 
				        city out of the hand of the king of Assyria: and I will defend this city. And this shall be a sign unto thee from the LORD, that 
				        the LORD will do this thing that he hath spoken; Behold, I will bring again the shadow of the degrees, which is gone down in the 
				        sun dial of Ahaz, ten degrees backward. So the sun returned ten degrees, by which degrees it was gone down. 
				        Isaiah 38:4-8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (630, 297, 'He died a peaceful death.', 'Behold therefore, I [God] will gather thee [Josiah] unto thy
				          fathers, and thou shalt be gathered into thy grave in peace;
				          and thine eyes shall not see all the evil which I will bring upon this
				          place. 2 Kings 22:20, 2 Chronicles 34:28', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (631, 297, 'He was killed in battle.', 'And king Josiah went against him; and he slew him at Megiddo,
				          when he had seen him. And his servants carried him in a chariot dead
				          from Megiddo, and brought him to Jerusalem. 2 Kings 23:29-30
				          
				        And the archers shot at king Josiah; and the king said to his
				          servants, Have me away; for I am sore wounded. His servants therefore
				          took him ... and brought him to Jerusalem, and he died. 2 Chronicles 35:23-24', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (632, 298, 'He was succeeded as king by his son.', 'So Jehoiachim slept with his fathers; and Jehoiachin his son
				          reigned in his stead. 2 Kings 24:6', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (633, 298, 'He had no one to succeed him.', 'Therefore thus saith the Lord of Jehoiakim king of Judah; He
				          shall have none to sit upon the throne of David. Jeremiah 36:30', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (634, 299, 'He was 18 years old and he reigned for 3 months.', 'Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. 2 Kings 24:8', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (635, 299, 'He was 8 years old and he reigned for 3 months and 10 days.', 'Jehoiachin was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned three months and ten days in Jerusalem. 2 Chronicles 36:9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (636, 300, 'Yes, his eyes beheld the king of Babylon.', 'Thine [Zedekiah''s] eyes shall behold the eyes of the king of
				          Babylon. Jeremiah 34:3', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (637, 300, 'No, his eyes were removed before he reached Babylon.', 'And they ... put out the eyes of Zedekiah, and bound him in
				          fetters of brass, and carried him to Babylon. 2 Kings 25:7', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (638, 301, 'On the seventh day', 'And in the fifth month, on the seventh day of the month
				          ... burned the house of the Lord. 2 Kings 25:8-9', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (639, 301, 'On the tenth day', 'Now in the fifth month, in the tenth day of the month
				          ... burned the house of the Lord. Jeremiah 52:12-13', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (640, 302, 'Five cubits', 'And the height of one chapiter was five cubits. Jeremiah 52:22', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (641, 302, 'Three cubits', 'The height of the chapiter was three cubits. 2 Kings 25:17', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (642, 303, 'Five men', 'And the captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest,
				          and Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the door.
				          And out of the city he took an officer that was set over the men of
				          war, and five men of them that were in the king''s
				          presence. 2 Kings 25:18-19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (643, 303, 'Seven men', 'And the captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest,
				          and Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the door ...
				          and seven men of them that were near the king''s person. Jeremiah 52:24-25', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (644, 304, 'On the 27th day of the month.', 'In the twelfth month, on the seven and twentieth day of the month, that Evilmerodach king of Babylon in the year that he began to reign did lift up the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah out of prison. 2 Kings 25:27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (645, 304, 'On 25th day of the month.', 'In the twelfth month, in the five and twentieth day of the month, that Evilmerodach king of Babylon, in the first year of his reign, lifted up the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah, and brought him forth out of prison. Jeremiah 52:31', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (646, 306, 'He was Josiah''s son.', 'And Josias begat Jechonias. Matthew 1:11', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (647, 306, 'He was Josiah''s grandson.', 'And the sons of Josiah were, the firstborn Johanan, the second Jehoiakim, the third
				    Zedekiah, the fourth Shallum. And the sons of Jehoiakim: Jeconiah his son. 1 Chronicles 3:15-16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (648, 307, 'Jeconiah was childless.', 'Thus saith the Lord, write this man [Jeconiah] childless .... No man of his seed shall prosper, sitting upon the throne of David, and ruling any more in Judah. Jeremiah 22:28-30', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (649, 307, 'Jeconiah had eight sons.', 'And the sons of Jeconiah; Assir, Salatheil his son, Malchiram also, and Pedaiah, and Shenazar, Jecamiah, Hoshama, and Nedabiah. 1 Chronicles 3.17-18:

The book of the generation of Jesus Christ ... Jeconiah begat Shealtiel ... And Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ. Matthew 1:1-16', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (650, 308, 'His father was Pedaiah.', 'And the sons of Pedaiah were, Zerubbabel, and Shimei. 1 Chronicles 3:19', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
INSERT INTO answers (id, contradiction_id, answer, answer_explanation, created_at) VALUES (651, 308, 'His father was Shealtiel.', 'Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel. Ezra 3:2, Nehemiah 12:1
				        
				      ... came the word of the LORD by Haggai the prophet unto Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel. Haggai 1:1
				    
				    
Salathiel begat Zorobabel. Matthew 1:12
				
				
Zorobabel, which was the son of Salathiel Luke 3:27', '2026-01-28 21:21:36');
